INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '0-fool', 'en', 'The Fool', '愚者', '{"keywords":["New Beginnings","Adventure","Innocence","Freedom","Trust"],"arcana":"major","number":0}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Fool symbolizes a fresh beginning and limitless possibility. This card suggests that you may be about to set out on an adventurous journey, meeting the unknown with an open mind and a sense of curiosity. It may be time to put down old baggage and welcome new experiences without assuming you already know how they will turn out. The Fool encourages you to take a first step even when the road ahead is uncertain. This is an energy of freedom and spontaneity, well suited to trying something new, learning a skill, or beginning a project. Stay lighthearted rather than becoming consumed by the outcome, and allow life to unfold as you move forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Fool invites you to be more careful and thoughtful. You may be making a rushed choice without considering its risks or consequences. This card can point to a lack of planning, an unclear direction, or an overly naive attitude that could make things harder for you. This may not be the moment to leap blindly; pause, assess the situation, and prepare what you need. You might be hesitating because you fear failure, or acting with so much confidence that you overlook important details. The reversed Fool suggests building a steadier foundation before you act and asking whether this choice truly fits you.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["New Beginnings","Adventure","Freedom","Innocence","Trust"],"reversed":["Recklessness","Indecision","Lack of Planning","Naivety","Fear"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Fool marks the beginning of a life journey and a willingness to explore without being ruled by prejudice or fear. As card zero, it holds many possibilities and has not yet been narrowed by experience. Its energy is light, free, and hopeful, like a child meeting the world with fresh curiosity. You do not need every answer at this stage; openness and flexibility may serve you better. The Fool’s step toward the cliff can look dangerous, yet it also represents trust in what cannot be seen. This is a leap-of-faith moment: you are invited to believe that the path can appear as you take your first steps.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Fool can show you wavering between two extremes: being so cautious that you miss an opportunity, or acting so impulsively that you are unprepared. Innocence may become naivety, while freedom may become a lack of direction. Past pain may make you afraid to take another chance, or overconfidence may keep you from seeing practical risks. Wisdom does not mean never taking a leap; it means looking at the situation before you do. Sometimes this card appears when you are ready but fear is keeping you in place. In that case, what you need may not be more preparation, but the courage to face the fear."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forward","type":"Outgoing and exploratory","description":"This is an outward-moving energy that explores the unknown. The Fool is curious and lively, taking steps without being bound by the past. Its flow is open and spontaneous rather than tightly controlled."},"timing":{"speed":"Fast","description":"Things may begin to unfold quickly, and an opportunity may arrive with little warning. This card favors taking a timely first step rather than waiting indefinitely. A noticeable beginning or change may appear within one to three weeks, though timing is never guaranteed."},"advice":{"upright":"Set fear aside, listen to your intuition, and take one first step. Your plan does not have to be perfect before you begin. Stay open to what you learn along the way and make room for the unexpected.","reversed":"Pause to assess the risks and make a basic plan before acting. Do not let an impulse make the decision for you; give yourself time to think it through. Ask someone you trust for another perspective and check for details you may have missed."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"You may feel disconnected from a sense of meaning or direction (crown), or lack the grounding and security needed to move forward (root).","healingNote":"If you feel afraid or stuck, grounding practices may help you reconnect with steadiness and safety. If you are acting recklessly, consider balancing reflection with practical planning. Crystal practices can be used as a personal ritual, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your inner voice may be calling you toward a new journey. This does not have to mean acting carelessly; it can be an invitation to trust your own wisdom and take the first step. You do not need to know the entire route before you begin. Many meaningful journeys start with one brave choice.","reversed":"This card invites you to practice wise courage. It is not asking you to remain still, but to connect with your inner judgment before you act. Freedom comes from clear awareness rather than a blind leap. Give yourself enough time to prepare, while noticing whether fear is keeping you from moving forward."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '1-magician', 'en', 'The Magician', '魔術師', '{"keywords":["Manifestation","Action","Focus","Creation","Resources"],"arcana":"major","number":1}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Magician suggests that you already have many of the tools and resources needed to pursue your goal. This card is associated with creativity and the ability to turn an idea into something tangible. You may have the skills, knowledge, and determination to take initiative and influence your surroundings. The Magician brings focus and action together: it is not only about imagining what could be, but also about choosing how to begin. Make use of the opportunities available to you, trust the abilities you have developed, and let your work speak for itself. Whether you are focused on a career, learning, or personal growth, a clear intention paired with practical effort can help you make meaningful progress.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Magician asks you to look carefully at how you are using your abilities and resources. You may be doubting your skills or struggling to put your ideas into practice. The card can also point to manipulation, dishonesty, or a temptation to take a shortcut, whether that behavior is coming from you or someone around you. Your effort may not be producing the outcome you expected, or you may feel unable to make use of what you have. Reconsider your motives and methods, and make sure your actions are honest and aligned with your values. Avoid trying to force an outcome through deception or misuse of influence; those approaches tend to create further problems.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Manifestation","Initiative","Focus","Creativity","Resources at Hand"],"reversed":["Manipulation","Self-Doubt","Misused Ability","Deception","Blocked Action"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Magician represents the ability to work with what is already available to you. The card’s central idea is, “I have something I can begin with.” You do not necessarily need to wait for perfect conditions or endless preparation; the skills and resources you have gathered can be put to use now. The Magician’s gesture between sky and ground is a symbol of connecting vision with practical action. When this energy is balanced, your attention is clear and your efforts have direction: you know what you are trying to make and can identify a next step. This is a moment to act thoughtfully rather than staying in planning mode. Let your intention guide your tools, while remaining open to feedback from the real world.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Magician can indicate that your abilities are being blocked or used in a way that does not reflect your values. You may have useful tools but feel unqualified to use them, or you may be attempting to control an outcome through pressure, deception, or a shortcut. The creative energy of the Magician can turn into cleverness used to avoid an honest conversation. You might feel like an impostor, or you might overestimate your ability to control circumstances and other people. This card invites you to look at the difference between influence and manipulation. Real capability includes recognizing limits, asking for help, and being truthful about what you can offer. If your efforts are not working, return to honesty and humility, then choose a more grounded approach."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"From vision into action","type":"Focused expression and transformation","description":"The Magician connects an idea with a practical form. Attention gathers around a clear intention and moves toward concrete action. This is active, creative energy: instead of waiting for every opportunity to arrive, you can make a deliberate opening for one."},"timing":{"speed":"Fast-moving","description":"A situation may begin to move quickly once you take action. The Magician favors getting started and making timely use of an opportunity. Early signs of progress may appear within one or two weeks, though this is a reflective timing cue rather than a guarantee."},"advice":{"upright":"Begin with the resources you already have. You do not need to wait for a perfect moment. Choose a clear goal, focus on the next practical step, and trust yourself enough to try. Let your actions show what you can do.","reversed":"Pause and review your motives before acting. Do not rely on pressure, manipulation, or misleading promises to get the result you want. Rebuild confidence by being honest about both your strengths and the areas you still need to develop."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra","issue":"You may feel unsure of your personal agency, struggle to express confidence, or try to control too much when you do not feel secure.","healingNote":"The Solar Plexus is commonly associated with agency and self-confidence. If you feel powerless or overly controlling, grounding routines and realistic goals may help you reconnect with your sense of choice. Crystals such as citrine or tiger’s eye can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your inner wisdom may be reminding you that you already have a place to begin. This is less about collecting one more tool and more about using what you have learned. You can choose how to direct your attention and effort. As you take a thoughtful step, notice what becomes possible through your own participation.","reversed":"The reversed Magician invites you to remember that lasting influence comes from integrity, not control. If you gain something by misleading someone, trust may be damaged and the result may not last. Be willing to look honestly at the parts of yourself you would rather hide, acknowledge what you still need to learn, and rebuild your confidence from a more truthful foundation."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '2-high-priestess', 'en', 'The High Priestess', '女祭司', '{"keywords":["Intuition","Wisdom","Mystery","Subconscious","Inner Knowing"],"arcana":"major","number":2}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The High Priestess embodies wisdom and intuition, guarding the realms of hidden knowledge and the subconscious. When this card appears, it reminds you to listen to your inner voice and trust your intuition. This is not a time to rely only on logical analysis; go deeper and explore the wisdom within. The High Priestess encourages meditation and a connection with your spiritual self so that you can find answers inwardly. This period may support the study of esoteric subjects, spiritual practice, or a deeper understanding of your subconscious. Remain patient and receptive, because some things need time to be revealed. The High Priestess also represents secrets and hidden knowledge, reminding you that some information may not yet be fully visible.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed High Priestess suggests that you may be ignoring your intuition or allowing external noise to drown out your inner voice. You may be relying too heavily on rational thought while suppressing your emotional and spiritual sides. This card can also suggest that a secret is being withheld or that you are refusing to see important information. You may feel disconnected from your inner wisdom and unable to access a deeper understanding. Rebuild your connection with intuition through time alone and honest reflection. The reversed High Priestess also asks you to face yourself truthfully rather than hiding the truth or avoiding deep feelings. Balance reason and feeling so that you can make the wisest decision.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Intuition","Inner Wisdom","Mystery","Waiting","Receiving Messages"],"reversed":["Ignoring Intuition","Overthinking","Hidden Secrets","Disconnection from Self","Unclear Information"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the High Priestess is a gateway to subconscious and spiritual wisdom. Seated between the black and white pillars, she guards hidden knowledge and symbolizes the balance of opposites behind a veil of mystery. This card asks you to stop searching outward and turn inward instead. Your intuition may be more reliable than logic right now, and your dreams may reveal more than your waking thoughts. The High Priestess does not offer answers immediately; she waits until you are ready to receive them. This is a quiet, inward, receptive energy, better suited to observing, waiting, and listening than taking action. The answer will emerge naturally at the right time.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed High Priestess shows that your connection with inner wisdom may have been severed. The noise of the outside world may be so loud that you cannot hear your inner voice. You may be relying on rational analysis to calculate every step while ignoring intuitive guidance. This card can also indicate a hidden secret or a truth you have chosen not to see. You may be afraid to face what lies within, using busyness to avoid being alone. The High Priestess reminds you that the truth does not disappear because you refuse to look at it. Be honest with yourself and rebuild your inner connection. Turn down the outside noise so that you can hear your own wisdom."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Inward","type":"Receptive","description":"The High Priestess carries an inward, receptive energy that waits rather than pushes forward. Seated between the black and white pillars, she guards the doorway to the subconscious. This is the energy of stillness, observation, and receiving spiritual messages."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow","description":"This situation needs time to develop, so do not rush. The High Priestess suggests that the timing is not yet right and may bring a waiting period of one to three months. The answer will appear naturally at the right time; forcing it will only make things harder."},"advice":{"upright":"Do not make a decision yet. Quiet yourself and listen to your intuition. Spend time meditating, being alone, and observing. The answer is already within you, even if it has not reached your conscious mind. Stay patient and let the message come to you.","reversed":"Reconnect with your intuition. Reduce external noise, step away from social media, and give yourself a quiet space. If there is a secret, face it honestly. Do not keep avoiding your inner voice; it has been trying to tell you the truth."},"chakra":{"primary":"Third Eye Chakra","issue":"Your intuition may feel blocked, making it difficult to receive spiritual insight, or you may be relying too heavily on logical thinking.","healingNote":"The High Priestess is closely connected with the Third Eye Chakra, a center commonly associated with intuition and inner vision. If you feel disconnected from intuition or unable to receive insight, you may benefit from practices that create quiet and reflection. Crystals such as amethyst or labradorite can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the answer is not outside you, but within you. The wisdom you have been seeking is something you already know. Stop searching outward and return to inner stillness. In that silence, you may hear what the universe has been saying to you all along.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you have drifted too far from yourself. The noise of the outside world has drowned out what is true within you. It is time to face honestly the truth you have been avoiding. Your intuition is still there; you have simply chosen not to listen. Come back to yourself."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '3-empress', 'en', 'The Empress', '皇后', '{"keywords":["Abundance","Nurturing","Creativity","Beauty","Plenty"],"arcana":"major","number":3}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Empress embodies the energy of abundance, nourishment, and creativity. She represents the richness of nature and the loving care of the mother, bringing growth and prosperity to life. When this card appears, it can point to a harvest season approaching, whether through material plenty or emotional and spiritual fulfillment. The Empress encourages you to connect with nature, enjoy life''s beautiful offerings, and treat yourself and others with love and care. This is an excellent time to nurture a creative project, build a home, or tend to relationships. The Empress also represents sensual pleasure and artistic beauty, reminding you to appreciate harmony and the loveliness around you. Her energy is gentle yet powerful, bringing healing and growth so that everything can thrive when nourished by love.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Empress may show blocked creativity or a lack of nourishment. You may be relying too heavily on others, or caring for everyone else while neglecting your own needs. This card can also point to overprotection or a suffocating relationship, whether you are controlling someone or being controlled. You may feel disconnected from your creativity or feminine energy, or experience material and emotional scarcity. The reversed Empress asks you to restore the balance of self-care and learn to set healthy boundaries. Do not let responsibility for others overwhelm you, and do not control people out of fear of losing them. Reconnect with nature and your body, and cultivate self-love and self-worth so that you can genuinely offer love and support.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Abundance","Nourishment","Creativity","Feminine Energy","Harvest"],"reversed":["Scarcity","Overgiving","Blocked Creativity","Imbalance","Suffocating Relationship"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Empress represents the abundance of the Earth Mother: creation, nourishment, and unconditional love. She sits in nature among ripe fields and flowing water, symbols of life''s fullness and growth. This card brings the accepting, gentle, patient strength that allows things to flourish. The Empress does not force anything to grow; she provides the best environment and lets life develop in its own time. This is feminine energy expressed not through conquest or control, but through love and care. The upright Empress reminds you that abundance is part of your nature, not something you must struggle to earn. When you care for yourself well, plenty can flow toward you naturally.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Empress shows that nourishing energy has become unbalanced. You may care for others so intensely that you forget yourself and become an exhausted giver. Or you may have completely ignored your creativity and your need to be loved. Feminine energy can turn into suffocation and overprotection, leading you to control someone in the name of doing what is best for them. This card can also point to a lost connection with your body and the natural world, leaving you feeling empty and deprived. The reversed Empress reminds you that you cannot pour from an empty cup. Stop overgiving and give love to yourself first. True abundance comes from inner fullness, not external accumulation."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Outward expansion","type":"Nourishing expression","description":"The Empress flows like the generous energy of the Earth Mother. She nourishes and supports growth, allowing everything to thrive in love. This is creative energy, but it is not hurried; it patiently waits for the fruit to ripen."},"timing":{"speed":"Natural pace","description":"Things will develop at a natural pace, like a seed that needs time to sprout. You may see results within one to two months. Do not rush the process; let it grow in its own time."},"advice":{"upright":"Take good care of your body, mind, and spirit. Spend time in nature and enjoy beautiful things. This is a good time to create and nurture something, but be patient. Love yourself well so that your love can flow freely to others.","reversed":"Stop overgiving. You are not responsible for being everyone''s parent, so care for yourself first. If you feel deprived, look at whether you have been ignoring your own needs. Learn to say no and set clear boundaries."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Overgiving may be draining your Heart Chakra, or creative energy may be blocked in the Sacral Chakra.","healingNote":"The Empress connects the Heart Chakra, associated with love and giving, with the Sacral Chakra, associated with creativity. If overgiving has left you exhausted, your heart needs replenishment. If creativity feels stuck, gentle creative practices may help restore movement. Crystals such as rose quartz or moonstone can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you deserve to be nourished and to enjoy beautiful things. Life is not only about giving and working; it also includes receiving and enjoying. Allow yourself to be loved and allow abundance to flow toward you. You are a child of the Earth, and fullness is part of your nature.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you have forgotten how to receive. You are used to being the giver, but do not know how to accept. This imbalance is draining your energy. It is time to stop and give love to yourself first. You do not need to prove your worth through constant giving."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '4-emperor', 'en', 'The Emperor', '皇帝', '{"keywords":["Authority","Structure","Leadership","Stability","Paternal Wisdom"],"arcana":"major","number":4}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Emperor represents authority, structure, and stability. He embodies leadership, organizational ability, and the wisdom to create order. When this card appears, it reminds you to approach matters with reason and logic, and to establish clear rules and boundaries. The Emperor encourages you to take responsibility and lead with firmness and fairness. This can be a good time to build a career, make plans, or consolidate what you have achieved. His energy is steady and dependable, offering protection and a sense of security. He reminds you that discipline and determination, sustained through effort and perseverance, can help you work toward long-term goals. The Emperor also represents paternal wisdom and experience, offering practical advice and support.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Emperor warns that you may be becoming too authoritarian or controlling. You may be misusing power, treating others harshly, or becoming so rigid that you cannot adapt to change. This card can also point to a lack of discipline or direction, making it difficult to manage yourself or others effectively. You may be avoiding responsibility, struggling to lead, or resisting authority. The reversed Emperor asks you to find balance between control and flexibility. Do not let fear drive you to control everything, but do not abandon structure and order altogether. Exercise authority with greater openness and consideration, and respect other people''s autonomy. Also ask whether you rely too heavily on external authority while overlooking your own inner wisdom.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Authority","Structure","Self-Mastery","Leadership","Stability"],"reversed":["Overcontrol","Authoritarianism","Lack of Discipline","Avoiding Responsibility","Rigidity"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Emperor represents the stabilizing force of paternal energy, embodying order, authority, and the ability to build. He sits on a stone throne with rugged mountains behind him, symbols of an unshakable foundation. This card brings rational, logical, and strategic thinking. Rather than relying on emotion or intuition, the Emperor makes decisions through experience and wisdom. He establishes rules, sets boundaries, and creates structure so that things can be kept in order. This is masculine energy expressed through leadership and control in the service of protection and stability. The upright Emperor reminds you that sometimes you must be the sovereign of your own life, creating an order and discipline that are truly yours.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Emperor shows that the energy of authority has become distorted or is missing. You may be excessively controlling, using strict rules to pressure yourself or others and turning protection into constraint. At the other extreme, you may lack discipline and direction, avoid responsibilities you need to take on, or struggle to lead. Paternal energy can become authoritarian and oppressive, with disagreement silenced in the name of doing what is best for everyone. This card can also point to resistance to authority and a rejection of all rules and structure. The reversed Emperor reminds you that true strength is not control, but flexibility within stability. Seek a balance between order and freedom."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Top-down","type":"Constructive leadership and control","description":"The Emperor''s energy directs and builds from the top down; it is a guiding, masculine force. He establishes order, sets rules, and takes charge. This is steady, practical, and methodical energy."},"timing":{"speed":"Steady and gradual","description":"Things are likely to move forward steadily according to plan rather than happen suddenly. The Emperor represents long-term building, and it may take two to six months to see solid results. This is a marathon, not a sprint."},"advice":{"upright":"Create a clear plan and structure. Set boundaries and take responsibility for leading. What is needed now is discipline and strategy, not emotion or impulse. Think like a CEO and make decisions rationally.","reversed":"Loosen your need for control. You cannot control everything, and you do not need to. Consider whether you are controlling others in the name of protecting them. If you have been too undisciplined, this may be the time to establish some structure. Look for balance."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"Your sense of power may be out of balance: you may be trying to control too much or feel completely out of control, with insecurity driving the need to take charge.","healingNote":"The Emperor connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power, and the Root Chakra, associated with security. Excessive control often comes from inner insecurity. If you need to control everything to feel safe, it may be worth tending to your sense of grounding. Practices involving crystals such as obsidian or red jasper can be used as a personal ritual for cultivating security. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade; crystal practices are not medical treatment, so consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that true strength comes from a stable foundation. You have the ability to build your own empire, but it takes patience and strategy. Take responsibility instead of avoiding it. You are more capable of directing your circumstances than you may think.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that control can be another expression of fear. If you need to manage everything before you can feel at ease, you may not be trusting life''s flow. Or are you avoiding a responsibility that is yours to carry? True strength is not control, but trust rooted in stability."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '5-hierophant', 'en', 'The Hierophant', '教皇', '{"keywords":["Tradition","Education","Faith","Mentor","Wisdom"],"arcana":"major","number":5}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hierophant represents traditional wisdom, spiritual teachers, and formal learning. He safeguards cultural, religious, and social values, offering moral and spiritual guidance. When this card appears, you may be seeking deeper meaning and spiritual understanding. This is a time to learn from a mentor, join a community, or follow an established system. The Hierophant encourages you to respect traditions and customs and draw on the wisdom of those who came before you. This period is well suited to formal education, religious ceremonies, or spiritual guidance. The Hierophant also represents commitment and loyalty, and may relate to marriage, joining an organization, or another formal union. He reminds you of the importance of cultural inheritance and collective wisdom, as well as the stability that comes from following ethical principles.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hierophant suggests that you may be challenging tradition or questioning an established belief system. You want to follow your own path rather than blindly obey rules set by others. This card may point to rebellion, unconventional ideas, or distrust of authority. You may feel that the current system is too rigid to meet your needs and values. The reversed Hierophant encourages you to develop your own beliefs and philosophy instead of following external dogma without question. At the same time, it cautions you not to oppose something merely for the sake of opposition; consider your path carefully. As you pursue personal freedom, remain open to the value of some traditional wisdom. Finding balance between respect for tradition and personal innovation can help you forge a path of your own.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Tradition","Mentor","Learning","Belief System","Formal Commitment"],"reversed":["Rebellion","Questioning Authority","Breaking with Tradition","Personal Beliefs","Spiritual Freedom"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hierophant represents the transmission of traditional wisdom and spiritual authority. He is a bridge between heaven and earth, the sacred and the everyday, safeguarding the values of culture, religion, and society. This card brings formal learning, a mentor''s guidance, and respect for established principles. The Hierophant does not forge a new path; he points toward roads that have been tested by those before you. This is a time to learn from tradition and deepen your understanding through ceremony, education, or commitment. The upright Hierophant reminds you that not every wheel needs to be reinvented. Standing on the shoulders of those who came before, you can see farther.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hierophant shows that you are questioning or rejecting external authority and tradition. You may feel that an established belief system no longer meets your spiritual needs, or that customary practices are limiting your growth. This rebellious energy can be liberating, but it can also become indiscriminate. You may be forming your own beliefs and no longer need a mentor or religion to tell you what is true. Yet this card also cautions against opposing things simply for the sake of opposition or becoming a cynical rebel. The reversed Hierophant reminds you that spiritual freedom does not mean rejecting every tradition; it means wisely choosing what suits you and what you are ready to release."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Passed down from mentor to student","type":"Teaching and receiving","description":"The Hierophant''s energy is one of transmission, flowing from teacher to student and from tradition to the present. It is the energy of learning, receiving guidance, and becoming part of a system. This is not about innovation, but about absorbing wisdom that already exists."},"timing":{"speed":"Follows an established process (moderate to slow)","description":"Matters are likely to proceed according to traditional or formal steps rather than move quickly. Formal commitments, education, or certification may take three to six months. Following the right steps matters more than speed."},"advice":{"upright":"Seek guidance from a mentor or qualified expert. Rather than trying to work everything out alone, learn from someone with experience. Follow established rules and processes instead of looking for shortcuts. If you are making a commitment, such as marriage or signing a contract, this may be a favorable time.","reversed":"Question the rules you have always followed: do they truly fit you? Do not follow tradition or authority blindly, but do not oppose them just for the sake of it. Choose your own path thoughtfully and build a belief system of your own."},"chakra":{"primary":"Throat Chakra and Crown Chakra","issue":"Difficulty expressing your authentic beliefs (Throat Chakra), or following external authority blindly and losing connection with your higher self (Crown Chakra).","healingNote":"The Hierophant connects the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression, and the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual connection. If you cannot express your beliefs or follow another''s doctrines blindly, these chakras may need balance. Lapis lazuli and clear quartz can support authentic spiritual expression through crystal practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that learning from those who came before you does not mean losing yourself. There is wisdom in tradition; do not overlook a path that has already proven effective just to be different. Find a mentor you can trust and let yourself stand on the shoulders of giants.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that no external authority can define your spiritual truth. The answers you seek are not in any religion or with any mentor; they are within you. It is time to reclaim your spiritual sovereignty and build a belief system of your own."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '6-lovers', 'en', 'The Lovers', '戀人', '{"keywords":["Love","Choice","Harmony","Partnership","Union"],"arcana":"major","number":6}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Lovers represents deep connection, harmony in relationships, and important choices. It symbolizes not only romantic love, but also deep bonds and partnerships of many kinds. When this card appears, it may point to an important decision that calls for you to stay true to your values and beliefs. The Lovers encourages you to seek harmony and balance, and to build mutual respect and understanding in your relationships. This can be a time to deepen intimacy, form an important partnership, or make a choice aligned with your values. The card also represents inner integration, bringing opposing parts together into a harmonious whole. The Lovers reminds you that love begins with self-acceptance: only when you can be authentically yourself can you build a truly deep and meaningful connection.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Lovers may point to imbalance, misunderstanding, or conflicting values in a relationship. You may be going through difficulties and feeling out of harmony with a partner or someone important to you. This card can also reflect confusion around an important decision, difficulty choosing, or a choice that does not align with your deepest wishes. You may have compromised your values or lost a sense of yourself in a relationship. The reversed Lovers asks you to reconsider your relationships and choices and make sure they reflect your core values. Do not sacrifice your authenticity just to please someone else. This is also a time to reflect on inner conflict and disharmony, practice self-love, and make choices that genuinely fit who you are.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["True Love","Soulmate","Aligned Values","Important Choice","Inner Integration"],"reversed":["Conflicting Values","Relationship Imbalance","Difficulty Choosing","Self-Betrayal","Disharmony"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Lovers represents a soul-level connection and a meaningful choice. This is not only about romantic love, but about alignment: with another person, with your values, and with a higher purpose. In the imagery, the angel Raphael blesses the scene from above, symbolizing a sacred union. The upright card emphasizes choosing in a way that is true to yourself. Whether you are choosing a relationship, a job, or a direction in life, ask whether it aligns with your core values. The Lovers is not about compromise for its own sake; it is about two whole people choosing to walk together. The upright Lovers reminds you that real love helps you become more fully yourself rather than lose yourself.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Lovers points to conflicting values or imbalance in a relationship. You may be sacrificing your values to keep a relationship, or be caught in a connection where you cannot be yourself. In the imagery, the angel''s blessing is blocked, suggesting that the connection lacks a sense of sacred alignment. You may face a difficult choice and feel unable to decide because every option seems to betray part of you. Or you may have already chosen while knowing inwardly that the choice is not right for you. The reversed Lovers reminds you that if a relationship requires you to give yourself up in order to keep it, it is not true love. Be honest with yourself: do your choices reflect who you really are?"},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Mutual exchange","type":"Union and integration","description":"The Lovers'' energy is mutual, equal, and flows in both directions. It is not one person giving while the other receives; it is two currents meeting, integrating, and creating a new harmony. This is the energy of yin and yang and the unity of dualities."},"timing":{"speed":"A pivotal moment","description":"The Lovers signals that the time to decide is now. This is not a gradual process but a clear point of choice. Within the coming weeks, you may face or already be facing an important decision."},"advice":{"upright":"Make choices that stay true to your values. Do not compromise your core beliefs just to please others. If the question is about a relationship, make sure your values are aligned. Real love helps you become more fully yourself rather than lose yourself.","reversed":"Look at your relationship or choice: are you betraying yourself? Do not sacrifice your authenticity just to keep a relationship. If you cannot decide, ask yourself which choice helps you feel more like your true self."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra","issue":"Heart Chakra imbalance: you may be so open that you lose your boundaries, or so closed off that genuine connection feels difficult.","healingNote":"The Lovers centers on the Heart Chakra and the balance of giving and receiving love. If a relationship leaves you feeling depleted, your boundaries may need attention. If you find it difficult to connect deeply, you may want to explore what would help you feel safer opening up. Rose quartz and green aventurine can be used as personal reflection and grounding practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that true love is a recognition between souls. When you meet the right person or face the right choice, your soul will know. Do not analyze everything with your mind; listen to your heart. Real love does not require you to change who you are; it allows you to be your most authentic self.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that if you have to pretend in order to be loved, it is not true love. You deserve a relationship that lets you be freely yourself. Stop compromising your soul to maintain a connection that is not right for you. Sometimes the most loving choice you can make for yourself is to leave."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '7-chariot', 'en', 'The Chariot', '戰車', '{"keywords":["Victory","Willpower","Control","Progress","Determination"],"arcana":"major","number":7}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Chariot symbolizes victory, willpower, and unwavering determination. It shows how focus and self-discipline can help you overcome obstacles and reach your goals. The charioteer guides two opposing forces, representing the ability to integrate conflicting energies and move in a clear direction. When this card appears, success may be within reach, but it calls for a steady will and a clear aim. This is a time to act, show determination, and meet challenges directly. The Chariot encourages you to trust your abilities and not let outside distractions shake your resolve. With discipline and focus, you can steer your course toward your goals. The card can also signify travel and progress, whether through a literal journey or movement along your life''s path.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Chariot suggests that you may have lost your sense of direction or control. You may feel pulled by opposing forces and unable to make a decision or act consistently. It can also point to aggression, forcefulness, or a lack of self-discipline. You may be rushing toward a goal or trying to force an outcome, creating conflict and resistance. The reversed Chariot asks you to regain your inner balance and direction. Do not let outside pressure or inner conflict keep you from moving forward. Meet challenges with greater flexibility and openness instead of pushing ahead at all costs. Pause to reassess your goals and methods, make sure you are on the right path, and choose a more harmonious way to pursue them.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Victory","Willpower","Steering Your Course","Breakthrough","Strong Momentum"],"reversed":["Loss of Control","Unclear Direction","Aggression","Inner Conflict","Lack of Discipline"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Chariot represents victory achieved through willpower and self-discipline. The charioteer guides two contrasting forces, symbolizing the integration of opposing energies in pursuit of a clear goal. This card is about taking charge—not controlling the outside world, but directing your own energy and course. You know where you want to go and have the resolve to face obstacles along the way. The Chariot advances through will and focus rather than brute force. It reminds you that when you are internally aligned and your aim is clear, the way forward becomes easier to see. This is a moment to commit yourself fully; victory is within reach.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Chariot shows a loss of direction or control. Opposing forces pull you apart, leaving you unable to move forward. You may be pushing too aggressively and creating more resistance, or you may have lost momentum and become stuck. Perhaps you have a goal but cannot follow through, or you are acting decisively in the wrong direction. Before charging ahead, bring your inner opposites into alignment. Hesitation and excessive force can both come from inner division. Pause, recalibrate your direction, and then begin again."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forward momentum","type":"Focused breakthrough","description":"The Chariot''s energy is highly focused and moves powerfully in one direction. It breaks through barriers, overcomes resistance, and advances toward a goal. This energy is linear, purposeful, and undivided."},"timing":{"speed":"Rapid progress","description":"Matters may develop quickly, with noticeable progress. The Chariot marks a period of acceleration, and a significant breakthrough may appear within two to four weeks. Maintaining momentum is important."},"advice":{"upright":"Give your full effort without getting distracted. This is a time to act, not just plan. Stay focused and direct your energy toward one clear aim. Victory calls for discipline and determination, so keep going.","reversed":"Pause and reassess your direction. Resolve the inner conflict that is pulling you in different ways. Do not try to force your way through; first bring your opposing impulses into alignment. If you have become too passive, this may also be a time to rebuild your momentum."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Low willpower or overexertion that leads to fatigue, with blocked motivation or difficulty taking action.","healingNote":"The Chariot connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with willpower, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with movement and vitality. If you feel unable to move forward or are pushing yourself into exhaustion, these centers may need balance. Citrine and amber can be included in personal grounding or reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you can achieve what you truly set your heart on. When your will is aligned with your deeper self, obstacles need not define your path. This is not the moment to doubt yourself, but to give your effort wholeheartedly. Trust yourself and keep moving; victory is yours to pursue.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that inner conflict is pulling you apart. One part of you wants to move forward while another resists. Before you can make real progress, bring these opposing parts into conversation. Or ask whether you are applying effort in the wrong direction. Listen inwardly, and you can find where you truly want to go."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '8-strength', 'en', 'Strength', '力量', '{"keywords":["Courage","Patience","Compassion","Inner Strength","Self-Control"],"arcana":"major","number":8}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Strength is not about brute force; it is about gentleness, patience, and inner courage. This card shows the ability to meet instinct with love and compassion rather than domination. When Strength appears, it reminds you that real strength comes from within—from accepting and understanding yourself and others. This is a time to be courageous, face your fears, and meet challenges with gentle resolve. Strength encourages you to trust your inner resources; you do not need force or violence to reach your goals. With patience, self-restraint, and compassion, you can work through obstacles. The card also speaks to emotional steadiness and resilience, reminding you to remain calm and graceful even in difficult moments. True strength transforms fear through love and eases conflict through understanding.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Strength card may point to a period of self-doubt, vulnerability, or low confidence. Fear and insecurity may be keeping you from expressing your real strength. It can also indicate excessive force or impatience: you may be trying to control a situation through pressure rather than guiding it gently. The reversed card asks you to reconnect with your inner courage and resources. Do not let outside criticism or inner fear erode your confidence. Treat yourself with compassion and patience, and accept your flaws and imperfections. Real strength comes from accepting and integrating every part of yourself, including the parts you consider weak. Through self-acceptance and inner peace, you can rediscover your strength.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Inner Strength","Gentle Resolve","Emotional Steadiness","Courage","Compassion"],"reversed":["Self-Doubt","Low Confidence","Excessive Force","Loss of Composure","Inner Conflict"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Strength shows the wisdom of the woman who meets the lion without force, guiding it with patience and care. Its central message is that real strength integrates rather than suppresses. You can face your instincts and fears not by fighting them, but by understanding and accepting them. This is emotional maturity: remaining calm in anger and courageous in fear. Strength embodies the wisdom that gentleness can overcome force; the more gently and firmly you respond, the more resilient you become. The inner beast is not your enemy, but a part of you waiting to be met with love. When you treat your shadow with compassion, you find a strength that cannot be shaken.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Strength suggests that you have lost touch with your inner resources. You may feel overwhelmed by fear and self-doubt, or use excessive force to hide your vulnerability, becoming controlling or domineering. The lion may be suppressed too deeply or allowed to roar unchecked. You may be harsh with yourself or others, replacing compassion with criticism. This card reminds you that real strength comes from inner balance, not outward domination. If you feel powerless, it may not be because you lack strength, but because you are using the wrong approach. Stop fighting yourself and begin making peace with who you are. True courage includes admitting vulnerability, and true strength can be gentle."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Integrated inward","type":"Balance and self-mastery","description":"Strength''s energy gathers inward, integrating instinct with conscious awareness. It is steady, sustained, gentle, and firm: not explosive, but enduring."},"timing":{"speed":"Steady over time","description":"Strength points to a process that calls for patience. Change may not happen overnight, but it can continue steadily. Building inner resilience and emotional steadiness may take two to three months."},"advice":{"upright":"Meet challenges with gentle resolve. Choose patience and care over force or pressure, and trust your inner strength to help you respond. Stay calm and treat yourself and others with compassion.","reversed":"Stop fighting yourself. Notice whether you are being too forceful or too hesitant, and look for a more balanced response. Accept your vulnerability and let care, rather than fear, guide you. Rebuild confidence in your inner resources."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra and Solar Plexus Chakra","issue":"A wounded Heart Chakra may make it difficult to respond with love, while imbalance in the Solar Plexus Chakra may show up as low confidence or excessive control.","healingNote":"Strength calls for balance between the Heart Chakra, associated with love and compassion, and the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power. If you feel powerless or overly forceful, these centers may need harmony. Rose quartz and citrine can be included in personal reflection or grounding practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you are stronger and gentler than you may realize. True strength is not about suppressing fear, but holding it with tenderness. When you stop fighting your instincts and learn to move with them, you discover a strength that cannot be shaken. Your gentleness is your strength.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you do not need to prove how strong you are, or pretend that you feel no fear. Real courage means admitting that you are afraid and choosing to move forward anyway. Stop using harshness to protect your vulnerability; let care help you meet your fear. Your strength is still there, though mistaken beliefs may have obscured it."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '9-hermit', 'en', 'The Hermit', '隱士', '{"keywords":["Introspection","Wisdom","Solitude","Truth","Guidance"],"arcana":"major","number":9}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hermit represents a period of introspection, solitude, and seeking inner truth. This card asks you to step back from the noise of daily life and give yourself quiet time to reflect and explore your inner world. The lantern in the Hermit''s hand symbolizes wisdom and guidance, illuminating the path toward truth. This can be a time for deep self-exploration, spiritual practice, or seeking a deeper sense of meaning. Solitude is not the same as loneliness; it can be an opportunity to reconnect with your authentic self. This period is well suited to study, reading, meditation, or other forms of inner work. The Hermit encourages you to trust your inner guidance and draw wisdom from your own experience. Through deep reflection, you can find answers to life''s questions and a direction for moving forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hermit suggests that you may be isolating yourself too much and refusing help or support. You may feel lonely and disconnected, or avoid social contact until you become closed off. This card can also point to excessive inward focus that causes you to overlook the needs and opportunities of the outside world. You may have built walls out of fear of being hurt or disappointed, but those walls can also limit growth and connection. The reversed Hermit asks you to find balance between solitude and social contact. Reflection matters, but complete isolation can lead to stagnation and discouragement. Try opening up and receiving other people''s support and perspectives. Sharing your thoughts and feelings can sometimes bring fresh insight and understanding.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Inner Wisdom","Spiritual Search","Solitary Reflection","Guiding Light","Deep Exploration"],"reversed":["Isolation","Rejecting Guidance","Avoiding Connection","Excessive Loneliness","Feeling Lost"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hermit represents a journey in search of wisdom deep within the soul. Standing on a mountaintop with a lantern, he symbolizes the insight that can come through reflection and solitude. This card calls you to step away from the noise of the outside world and enter a quieter inner sanctuary. The Hermit is not escaping; he is making space for a deeper connection. This can be an important period for seeking meaning and spiritual growth. You may need solitude to process past experiences, organize your thoughts, and listen to what matters within. The Hermit''s lantern first illuminates his own path, not someone else''s. When you find your own light, you may be able to offer guidance to others. The card reminds you that some answers are found not outside, but in the deepest part of yourself.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hermit suggests that solitude may have turned into avoidance. You may have built walls because you fear being hurt, refusing connection with the outside world. The Hermit can become a recluse who hides from life rather than seeking wisdom. You may feel intensely lonely and still hesitate to open up. This card can also point to ignoring your inner guidance, becoming so focused on the outside that you lose contact with yourself. Sometimes the reversed Hermit means your inner search has reached a natural pause and it is time to return to the world and share what you have learned. Balance is key: neither complete isolation nor constant outward activity is likely to serve you."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Deeply inward","type":"Receiving and reflecting","description":"The Hermit''s energy moves inward, like diving into the depths of the unconscious to find a pearl. It is quiet, contemplative, and exploratory, calling for solitude and stillness."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow and deepening","description":"The Hermit points to a process that takes time. Genuine wisdom cannot be rushed; a period of inner exploration and reflection may take three to six months. Let insight emerge naturally."},"advice":{"upright":"Give yourself time and space alone. Reduce social activity and make room for meditation, reading, and reflection. Look inward for answers instead of seeking them everywhere else. Trust that your inner wisdom can emerge in quiet moments.","reversed":"Ask whether you are choosing solitude or becoming isolated. If you have closed yourself off, try opening up and accepting support. If you have been constantly outward-facing, make some quiet time for yourself. Seek a balance between being alone and connecting with others."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra","issue":"Feeling disconnected from spiritual guidance or unable to receive insight, or becoming so absorbed in spiritual concerns that you lose touch with practical life.","healingNote":"The Hermit has a strong connection with the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual awareness. If you feel lost or unable to hear your inner guidance, you may want to explore practices that help you feel centered and present. Clear quartz and amethyst can be included in personal reflection rituals. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this may be a time to withdraw—not because you are weak, but because you need to recharge and find your direction. In stillness, you may hear a truth that has been overlooked. Your lantern is waiting for you to light it, and that calls for solitude and reflection. This is a part of the journey only you can walk.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that isolation is not strength; it can be fear. You may have hidden long enough, and it may be time to reconnect with the world. Or perhaps you have been out in the world for too long and need to return to yourself. Balance solitude with connection, and you can find a deeper wisdom."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '10-wheel', 'en', 'Wheel of Fortune', '命運之輪', '{"keywords":["Change","Fate","Cycles","Luck","Turning Point"],"arcana":"major","number":10}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Wheel of Fortune represents life''s cycles, change, and turning points. It reminds you that everything is in motion and nothing stays the same forever. When the Wheel appears, an important change may be approaching, bringing good fortune or a new opportunity. The card encourages you to accept life''s highs and lows as natural parts of a larger cycle. It also speaks to karma and cause and effect, reminding you that past actions can shape the present and future. This is a time to move with changing circumstances and make use of opportunities. Stay open and flexible, because change can bring growth and progress. Trust the unfolding of events, and keep faith through difficult moments: the Wheel continues to turn.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Wheel of Fortune suggests that you may be going through a difficult period or resisting a change that needs to happen. You may feel out of control, as though fate is directing your life without your input. This card can also point to bad luck or an unfavorable turn that leaves you discouraged or powerless. Even in difficulty, however, you can choose how to respond. Rather than becoming trapped in a victim mindset, look for ways to create change. This may be a time to reassess your circumstances and learn from what is challenging you. Remember that the Wheel does not stay at its lowest point forever; difficult periods pass. Be patient and resilient, and trust that circumstances can improve in time.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Turning Point","Karmic Cycle","Good Fortune","Timing for Change","Universal Order"],"reversed":["A Difficult Cycle","Resistance to Change","Bad Luck","Loss of Control","Karmic Reckoning"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Wheel of Fortune symbolizes life''s natural cycles and the arrival of a turning point. The Wheel keeps moving, reminding you that nothing lasts forever: highs pass, and so do lows. This card often signals good fortune and positive change, as circumstances may be turning in a more favorable direction. It can represent the results of past choices beginning to unfold. The Wheel encourages you to move with life''s flow rather than resist every change. When opportunity comes around, make use of it; when circumstances shift away, keep faith and allow another cycle to arrive. This card teaches you to accept life''s ups and downs as part of a larger pattern.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Wheel of Fortune suggests a low point or strong resistance to necessary change. The Wheel is still turning, but you may feel controlled by circumstances and unable to influence your life. This can be a period when past actions bring difficult consequences. Yet even at a low point, the Wheel will turn again. You are not powerless to choose your response. The reversed Wheel asks you to accept the circumstances you cannot immediately change and trust that they will also pass. Sometimes it is a prompt to create change actively instead of waiting passively."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Cyclical movement","type":"Transformation and change","description":"The Wheel of Fortune moves in cycles, like the changing seasons and rising and falling tides. This is the natural rhythm of the universe: you cannot control it entirely, but you can learn to understand and move with it. Energy shifts between highs and lows."},"timing":{"speed":"Sudden change","description":"The Wheel of Fortune points to an unexpected turning point. A change may occur suddenly within one to four weeks, often in a way that is difficult to predict. Timing may depend on circumstances beyond your control."},"advice":{"upright":"Move with changing circumstances and make use of the good fortune or opportunity available now. Stay open and flexible. Remember that every phase is temporary: appreciate what is here without clinging to it, and give thanks for what your past actions have made possible.","reversed":"Accept that a difficult period is temporary. Do not resist every change or become trapped in a victim mindset. Reflect on the results of your past choices and what you can learn from them. This is a time for learning and growth; keep faith that the Wheel will turn again."},"chakra":{"primary":"All Chakras, especially the Crown and Root Chakras","issue":"Difficulty accepting life''s cycles and changes, or feeling disconnected from a larger sense of order.","healingNote":"The Wheel of Fortune can be understood in relation to the whole energy system, especially the Crown Chakra, associated with connection to a larger order, and the Root Chakra, associated with grounding and surrender. If change feels impossible to accept or you feel out of control, grounding and balancing practices may help. Crystal practices can serve as a way to reconnect with a sense of rhythm. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this turning point is part of a larger timing. The good you have done may be opening new possibilities. Enjoy this moment of change, while remembering that the Wheel will keep turning. Learn to stay centered as things move and steady within yourself as circumstances change.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that a low point is not a punishment; it is part of life''s natural cycles. You may be working through the consequences of past choices and learning from them. The Wheel does not remain at its lowest point forever, but it can take patience to keep faith through difficulty. This challenge may be one step on the way toward a new high point."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '11-justice', 'en', 'Justice', '正義', '{"keywords":["Fairness","Truth","Cause and Effect","Balance","Law"],"arcana":"major","number":11}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Justice represents fairness, truth, and karmic balance. It reminds you that actions have consequences. When this card appears, it may be time to make a fair decision, or to face the results of past actions. Justice encourages honesty and integrity, and choices that align with your conscience and ethics. It can also relate to legal matters, contracts, and agreements, reminding you to make sure that terms are fair and transparent. This is a time to take responsibility, face the facts, and seek balance. The figure of Justice holds scales and a sword, symbols of objective judgment and decisive action. She asks you to think clearly, view matters without bias, and make the fairest decision you can.","reversedMeaning":"Reversed, Justice may point to unfairness, bias, or dishonesty. You may be treated unjustly, or you may not be acting with integrity yourself. This card can also indicate avoiding responsibility, refusing to admit a mistake, or struggling to judge a situation fairly. Bias may be making it difficult to see the truth objectively. The reversed Justice asks you to be honest about your actions and motives. If you have caused harm, take responsibility and make amends. If you are being treated unfairly, do not stay silent; speak up for yourself. The card can also point to legal or contractual disputes where professional guidance may be helpful. Begin restoring balance and fairness with honesty and accountability.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Fair Judgment","Truth and Consequences","Accountability","Balance","Honesty and Integrity"],"reversed":["Unfairness","Avoiding Responsibility","Bias","Dishonesty","Imbalance"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Justice represents balance and the principle of cause and effect. The scales and sword symbolize careful consideration followed by decisive action. This card reminds you that choices have consequences: what you set in motion can shape what follows. Justice asks you to look honestly at your decisions and behavior and accept your share of responsibility. It can also refer to legal matters, contracts, or important choices that call for objectivity and fairness. Justice is not revenge; it is the restoration of balance. Acting with honesty and integrity helps you make decisions you can stand behind. The card encourages you to trust that truth can come to light and fairness can be pursued.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Justice points to unfairness, bias, or an unwillingness to take responsibility. You may be treated unfairly, or you may be reluctant to acknowledge where your own actions have lacked integrity. The scales are out of balance: facts may be obscured and responsibility shifted elsewhere. You may be judging yourself or others through bias rather than looking objectively at what happened. This card can indicate avoiding consequences or refusing to admit a mistake. Avoidance can make a problem harder to resolve. Face the facts honestly and take responsibility for your part to begin restoring balance. If you are being treated unfairly, speak up for yourself. Truth may be hidden for a time, but it can still come to light."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Symmetrical balance","type":"Evaluation and adjustment","description":"Justice seeks a point of balance, like the two sides of a scale. Its energy is rational, objective, and measured rather than driven by emotion. It looks for fairness and truth by finding a center between opposing positions."},"timing":{"speed":"Governed by due process","description":"Justice reflects cause and effect, and timing may depend on when circumstances are ready to resolve. A fair outcome may become visible within one to three months, though it can take longer. Justice is not rushed, but resolution can come in time."},"advice":{"upright":"Act honestly and with integrity. Make a fair decision without favoring one side unfairly. Accept your responsibilities and expect others to accept theirs. Trust careful fact-finding and fairness. If you have a legal matter, seek appropriate professional advice about your situation.","reversed":"Look honestly at your behavior: are you avoiding responsibility? If you are being treated unfairly, speak up for yourself. Set aside bias and judgment so you can see the facts clearly. Acknowledge mistakes, make amends where appropriate, and work toward restoring balance."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Difficulty speaking up for yourself (Throat Chakra), or lacking the confidence to take responsibility (Solar Plexus Chakra).","healingNote":"Justice connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power and responsibility, and the Throat Chakra, associated with speaking truth. If it is difficult to tell the truth or take responsibility, these centers may need balance. Citrine and blue kyanite can be included in personal grounding or reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that fairness begins with the choices you make. You are now in a position to see the results of acting with integrity. Continue treating yourself and others honestly and fairly, and let your actions reflect what you believe. Truth is one of your greatest strengths.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that consequences cannot be avoided forever. What you set in motion will eventually have results. Be honest about your actions and take responsibility for your part. If you are being treated unfairly, do not stay silent; speak up for yourself. Restoring inner integrity is part of creating greater fairness in your life."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '12-hanged', 'en', 'The Hanged Man', '倒吊者', '{"keywords":["Pause","New Perspective","Letting Go","Sacrifice","Waiting"],"arcana":"major","number":12}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hanged Man represents a pause, letting go, and the wisdom of seeing things from a new perspective. It reminds you that sometimes stopping and changing your point of view is more valuable than pushing ahead. The Hanged Man willingly hangs from a tree, symbolizing a temporary sacrifice or devotion in service of a larger purpose. This is a period for reflection and waiting, not for forcing action. You may need to see a problem from a different angle to understand it. The Hanged Man encourages you to accept the present situation, even when it feels uncomfortable or counterintuitive. This period may suit spiritual practice, meditation, and inner exploration. By loosening your need for control and accepting uncertainty, you can gain new insight and wisdom. Sometimes letting go is the best way to move forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hanged Man suggests that you may be resisting a necessary pause or a change in perspective. You may feel stuck while also being unwilling to make a change that could shift the situation. This card can point to procrastination, needless sacrifice, or feeling trapped and unable to move forward. You may be attached to old ways of thinking and unwilling to look at the problem from a new angle. The reversed Hanged Man asks you to consider taking action to break the stalemate. If you have been waiting indefinitely, it may be time to do something. At the same time, the card cautions against changing merely for the sake of change or making a rushed decision. Look at what you are resisting and why you may be reluctant to shift your perspective. Sometimes accepting the present and waiting patiently is the wiser choice.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Surrender and Wait","Shift in Perspective","Pause and Reflect","Devotion","Release of Control"],"reversed":["Resistance and Stagnation","Procrastination","Needless Sacrifice","Rigid Thinking","Unwillingness to Change"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hanged Man represents a profound pause and a change in perspective. He hangs from a tree with a peaceful expression, symbolizing the wisdom that can come from surrendering and loosening control. This card asks you to stop struggling against circumstances you cannot change right now. This is not passive resignation, but an intentional choice to look at the situation differently. The Hanged Man reminds you that seeing the world upside down can reveal what you could not see before. This may be a time to set aside something smaller in service of a more meaningful insight. The waiting period has a purpose, and impatience may only prolong the process. The Hanged Man teaches growth in stillness and transformation through waiting.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hanged Man suggests that you may be resisting a necessary pause or caught in an unproductive standstill. You may refuse to change your perspective and cling rigidly to old ways of thinking. The pause can become procrastination, and sacrifice can become needless suffering. You may feel trapped while being unwilling to make a change that could break the stalemate. This card can also mean that you have waited long enough and it is time to act. Waiting has value, but waiting indefinitely can become avoidance. Ask whether you are waiting patiently or postponing action out of fear. Sometimes meaningful change begins with being willing to consider another possibility."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Stillness and pause","type":"Internalization and transformation","description":"The Hanged Man''s energy pauses and turns inward, like a pupa transforming inside a cocoon. The surface may appear still while deep inner change is taking place. This is the energy of surrender, acceptance, and turning your perspective around."},"timing":{"speed":"A period of delay and waiting","description":"The Hanged Man points to a clear waiting period. Matters may not move quickly and can call for two to six months of pause and reflection. This is an opportunity to practice patience; rushing may not change what needs time."},"advice":{"upright":"Stop struggling against the situation for now. Accept what is present and try looking at the problem from a different angle. This pause may be necessary, and patient reflection can bring deeper insight. Ask yourself what you may need to release.","reversed":"Ask whether you are waiting or procrastinating. If fear is keeping you from acting, consider taking a practical next step. If you have been resisting a different perspective, try turning the problem around and looking again. Breaking a stalemate may require a willingness to change how you think."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"Difficulty surrendering to a higher perspective (Crown Chakra), or an excessive need for control and security (Root Chakra).","healingNote":"The Hanged Man calls for balance between the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual surrender, and the Root Chakra, associated with grounded security. If it is difficult to release control or tolerate waiting, grounding and reflective practices may help. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders to build trust and patience. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this pause is not a punishment; it can be a gift. During this period of waiting, deep inner change may be taking place. Look at things from a different angle and you may notice a truth you had overlooked. Surrender is not giving up; it can be a deeper kind of wisdom. Trust the process and allow transformation to unfold.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you may have waited long enough, or may be unwilling to wait at all. If you have waited long enough, it may be time to act; if you are resisting the pause, practice surrender. Resistance can prolong discomfort. Sometimes the bravest step is to stop, become still, and look at everything with fresh eyes."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '13-death', 'en', 'Death', '死神', '{"keywords":["Transformation","Ending","Rebirth","Letting Go","Transition"],"arcana":"major","number":13}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Death card represents endings, transformation, and renewal, not literal death. It marks the close of an important phase and the beginning of another. When Death appears, it asks you to release the past and let what has run its course make room for new possibilities. This may involve ending a relationship, leaving a job, changing a belief, or releasing an old pattern of behavior. Change can feel unsettling, but Death points to necessary transformation and renewal. The card encourages you to accept life''s natural cycles and understand that endings make new beginnings possible. Death rides a white horse, symbolizing the purifying power of transformation. Rather than resist the process, meet change and trust that what follows can bring growth and evolution.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Death card suggests that you may be resisting a necessary ending or change. You may be clinging to people, situations, or things that no longer suit you because you fear that letting go means losing everything. This card can also point to stagnation and difficulty completing a transition. You may be caught between past and future, unable to release one or welcome the other. The reversed Death reminds you that refusing change can create more pain and difficulty. Some things have reached their end, and forcing them to continue can drain your energy. Be honest about what is happening and accept that something may need to end. Letting go is not failure; it creates room for something more fitting to enter your life. Allow yourself to grieve what you have lost, then find the courage to move forward.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Profound Transformation","Ending and Rebirth","Releasing the Past","Renewal","Necessary Endings"],"reversed":["Resisting an Ending","Unable to Let Go","Stagnation","Fear of Change","Slow Transition"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Death represents deep and complete transformation: one cycle ends so another can begin. The white horse symbolizes a purifying force that carries away what is outdated or no longer serves you. This card asks you to accept the close of an important phase, whether it involves a relationship, work, a belief, or a way of living. It does not refer to literal death, but to symbolic ending and renewal. Death reminds you that something new can emerge when the old has ended. This transformation may be painful, but it can also be necessary, and resisting it may prolong the pain. Death teaches you to release attachment and trust the process of change. Beyond an ending, renewal remains possible.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Death suggests strong resistance to a necessary ending or transition. You may be holding on to something that has run its course because you fear loss or the unknown. The ending may be delayed, but resisting it can create further pain and stagnation. You may feel suspended between past and future, unable to release one or welcome the other. This card can also point to such a strong fear of change that you will do almost anything to preserve the status quo. The reversed Death reminds you that some things have reached their end, and forcing them to continue can drain your life energy. Letting go is not failure; it can be an act of wisdom. When you allow an ending to happen, renewal becomes possible."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Clearing and release","type":"Transformation and rebirth","description":"Death''s energy clears and releases, like autumn leaves making room for spring growth. This is an irreversible kind of transformation: the old must end for something new to begin. Energy moves from an ending toward renewal."},"timing":{"speed":"An unavoidable ending","description":"Death points to an ending whose timing is shaped by life itself. A period of transition may take one to three months, while full renewal may take longer. What is ready to end cannot always be hastened or delayed."},"advice":{"upright":"Accept the ending instead of resisting it. Release people, situations, or habits that no longer fit your life. Trust the process of change, even if you cannot yet see what comes next. Give yourself room to grieve, then take a brave step forward.","reversed":"Be honest about what you are holding on to and why it is hard to release. Fear is natural, but it does not have to prevent necessary change. Some things must end; accepting that sooner can help you begin a new chapter sooner."},"chakra":{"primary":"Root Chakra and whole-system clearing","issue":"Fear of loss may unsettle your sense of security, or your overall energy may feel in need of deep clearing.","healingNote":"Death''s transformation can affect the whole energy system, especially the Root Chakra, associated with survival and security. If it is difficult to accept an ending or transition, rebuilding a sense of safety and trust may help. Obsidian and smoky quartz can be included in personal practices for reflection and release. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this ending may be a necessary blessing. What you have been holding on to has fulfilled its purpose, and it may be time to let go. Death is not the end, but a doorway to transformation. As you release what is complete, new life can begin. Trust the process; renewal is waiting on the other side.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you cannot remain between two worlds forever. What has reached its end must be allowed to end; resisting it can deepen the pain. Letting go does not mean losing everything; it can make room for what truly matters. Stop fighting life''s natural movement and allow change to take place. Renewal is waiting on the other side."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '14-temperance', 'en', 'Temperance', '節制', '{"keywords":["Balance","Adjustment","Patience","Harmony","Moderation"],"arcana":"major","number":14}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Temperance represents balance, harmony, and the wisdom of moderation. The image of an angel pouring water between two cups symbolizes energy moving and blending. When Temperance appears, it reminds you to seek balance and harmony in different areas of life. This may mean bringing opposing elements together, balancing work and personal life, or making room for both reason and emotion. Temperance encourages patience and self-restraint, and cautions against extremes and excess. This is a time for healing, adaptation, and integration, calling for gentle, gradual progress. Temperance also represents spiritual alchemy: different elements becoming a harmonious whole. It reminds you that moderation has wisdom and that enough can be enough. With patience and adjustment, you can cultivate inner peace and greater harmony around you.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Temperance card suggests imbalance, excess, or a lack of moderation. You may be putting too much energy into one area while neglecting other important parts of life. This card can also point to impatience and a desire for quick results that leads you to skip necessary steps. You may feel disharmony within yourself or in your surroundings, unable to bring opposing elements together. The reversed Temperance asks you to find your balance again. Review your life and notice where there may be too much or too little. Practice moderation and avoid swinging to extremes. This card may also caution against overindulgence in a habit or behavior that calls for greater self-control. Take time to adjust gently. Remember that balance is not a final destination, but an ongoing process.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Harmonious Balance","Moderation","Integration","Patient Progress","Alchemy"],"reversed":["Imbalance and Excess","Lack of Moderation","Extremes","Impatience","Difficulty Integrating"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Temperance represents the art of integration and balance, like alchemy. An angel pours water between two cups, one associated with active energy and the other with receptive energy, symbolizing opposing elements blending in harmony. This card teaches the wisdom of moderation: avoid extremes and find a point of balance among different forces. Temperance is not suppression, but harmonizing what is present. This is a time for healing and integration, as seemingly conflicting parts of life are brought into a more coherent whole. Temperance asks you to be patient and make gradual progress. Real strength is not found in extremes, but in balance. When you find your center, you can work with change more skillfully.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Temperance suggests imbalance and excess. You may be investing too much in one area and neglecting other important needs, or swinging sharply between extremes. The energy of integration is blocked, making it hard for opposing elements to coexist peacefully. You may be impatient for results and skip steps that matter. This card can also point to overindulgence in a habit or behavior and difficulty exercising self-control. The reversed Temperance reminds you that imbalance can cause distress. Look honestly at where there is too much and where there is not enough. Healing takes time and patience; it cannot be forced to happen all at once. Return to your center and find balance again."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Two-way flow and integration","type":"Harmonizing and balancing","description":"Temperance''s energy flows in both directions, building a bridge between opposing forces. It is gentle, gradual, and continually adjusting, seeking dynamic balance rather than rigid stillness. Energy transforms through integration."},"timing":{"speed":"Gradual and unhurried","description":"Temperance represents a gradual process that calls for time and patience. Genuine integration and balance cannot be rushed and may take two to four months of ongoing adjustment. Take your time; steady work matters."},"advice":{"upright":"Seek the middle path and avoid extremes. Find balance between work and personal life, reason and emotion, and giving and receiving. Be patient and make changes gently. Integrate opposing parts instead of forcing yourself to choose only one side.","reversed":"Look at where your life may be out of balance. What is receiving too much attention, and what is being neglected? Practice moderation and self-control. Do not rush results; give yourself time to adjust gradually. Return to your center and rebuild harmony."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra","issue":"Heart Chakra imbalance may make it difficult to integrate opposing energies or may pull you too strongly toward one extreme.","healingNote":"Temperance is closely connected with the Heart Chakra''s role in balance and integration, bridging the upper and lower energy centers. If you feel out of balance or unable to reconcile conflicting needs, this center may benefit from care. Rose quartz and green aventurine can be included in personal reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the art of life is balance, not perfection. You are learning an alchemy that turns opposites into harmony. Be patient; the middle path can be a powerful one. You do not have to choose one side when you can integrate both. In balance, you may discover a truer sense of yourself.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you may have lost your center. Excess and deprivation are both forms of imbalance. Pause and look honestly at your life; you cannot keep swinging between extremes. Healing comes through gentle adjustments rather than drastic changes. Return to your center and begin again from there."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '15-devil', 'en', 'The Devil', '惡魔', '{"keywords":["Bondage","Addiction","Materialism","Dependency","Limitations"],"arcana":"major","number":15}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Devil represents bondage, addiction, and the pull of material desire. The figures on the card are chained, but the chains are loose, suggesting that some constraints are self-imposed and may be possible to loosen. When this card appears, you may feel trapped by a habit, belief, or relationship. This could involve substance use, a harmful relationship, compulsive behavior, or a limiting pattern of thought. The Devil also represents the shadow self and suppressed desires, asking you to face deep fears and parts of yourself you have kept hidden. This card is not here to judge you; it is meant to bring awareness to what may be controlling you. Once you can recognize a bond, you can begin to consider your choices and seek support to loosen it. The Devil reminds you that change and greater freedom are possible.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Devil is often an encouraging sign of beginning to break free from constraints, move toward release, and see more clearly. You may be working to change an addictive pattern, leave a harmful relationship, or challenge a limiting belief. This card suggests that you are starting to see through an illusion. However, the reversed Devil can also point to denying that a problem exists or underestimating the hold a pattern has on you. You may tell yourself everything is fine while remaining caught in an unhealthy cycle. The reversed Devil reminds you that release is a process requiring courage and honesty. Do not be afraid to face your shadow; accepting and integrating it can help you move toward freedom. This can be a powerful time of change and an opportunity to take greater ownership of your life. If addiction or safety is involved, professional and trusted support can be an important part of that process.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Self-Imposed Bondage","Addiction and Dependency","Material Temptation","Shadow Self","False Security"],"reversed":["Breaking Free","Awakening and Release","Changing Addictive Patterns","Facing the Shadow","Breaking Limitations"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Devil reveals bonds and limitations that may have been created or reinforced by your own choices. The figures are held by loose chains, suggesting that a way out may exist even if it is not yet easy to see. This card asks you to notice what is controlling you: an addictive pattern, a harmful relationship, material desire, a limiting belief, or an excessive need for security. The Devil represents the shadow parts of yourself—the desires and fears you may not want to admit. It is not a judgment, but an invitation to become aware. Recognizing what binds you is the first step toward choosing what to do about it. The Devil reminds you that a prison can be built from your own beliefs, and that the possibility of freedom begins with seeing the key you already hold.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Devil often signals that you are beginning to break free and see clearly what has been controlling you. You may be loosening old chains, changing an addictive pattern, leaving a harmful relationship, or challenging limiting beliefs. Yet the reversed Devil can also indicate continued denial or the belief that you are free when the same pattern has simply taken another form. Genuine release takes courage and honesty about your vulnerabilities. The more clearly you can see the bond, the more consciously you can choose how to respond."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Heavy and downward","type":"Bondage and limitation","description":"The Devil''s energy feels dense and heavy, as though pulled downward by gravity. It can feel sticky and difficult to escape, leaving you trapped or powerless. Energy is confined to material concerns and struggles to rise."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow and stuck","description":"The Devil represents feeling trapped, where time itself may seem distorted. Breaking a pattern calls for awareness and sustained effort and may take three to six months or longer. Change will not happen automatically; it asks you to take active steps to interrupt the cycle."},"advice":{"upright":"Be honest about what is binding you. Stop telling yourself, “I can quit whenever I want,” without examining the pattern. Face your shadow, acknowledge your vulnerabilities and desires, and remember that a chain can sometimes be loosened. Ask yourself why you are choosing to stay. If addiction, abuse, or safety is involved, reach out to qualified and trusted support rather than facing it alone.","reversed":"If you are working to break free, keep going and seek support when you need it. If you are denying a problem, this is a time to face it honestly. Breaking an old pattern takes courage and persistence. You do not have to do it alone; acknowledging what is happening is a meaningful first step."},"chakra":{"primary":"Root Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Excessive attachment to material security (Root Chakra), or feeling controlled by desire and compulsive patterns (Sacral Chakra).","healingNote":"The Devil relates to imbalance in the lower energy centers, especially the Root Chakra, associated with fear and security, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with desire and pleasure. If you feel trapped or unable to change a pattern, grounding and reflective practices may help you explore what is happening. Obsidian and smoky quartz can be included in personal practices for reflection and release. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you may be freer than you think. The chains that bind you may be loose, and a choice may be available—but first you have to acknowledge the chains are there. Do not be afraid to see your shadow; it is a part of you that needs care and acceptance. You still have the power to choose your next step.","reversed":"Your soul is celebrating your awakening: you are working to break free and reclaim your choices. This path may not be easy, but you have begun. Do not let old comforts pull you back into the same pattern. True freedom lies ahead. Or perhaps your soul is reminding you to stop denying the problem: you may not be fully free yet, but caught in a different form of the same cage. Be honest with yourself."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '16-tower', 'en', 'The Tower', '高塔', '{"keywords":["Sudden Change","Upheaval","Revelation","Destruction","Awakening"],"arcana":"major","number":16}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Tower represents sudden change, disruption, and moments of awakening. The lightning-struck tower symbolizes structures built on unstable foundations beginning to collapse. When this card appears, a dramatic shift may be approaching, perhaps through a startling revelation, an unexpected event, or problems that have been building over time finally surfacing. Although the change may be painful and unsettling, it can clear away what no longer serves you and make room for something more genuine and stable. The Tower reminds you that sometimes a system needs a complete reset before it can be rebuilt on firmer ground. This is a moment of awakening and truth coming to light. Even when the process is difficult, it can create room for release and growth. Accept what needs to be dismantled and remain open to new possibilities emerging from the ruins.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Tower suggests that you may be avoiding or delaying a necessary change or breakdown. You may sense a major shift coming and try to prevent or control it. Fear of change may be so strong that you would rather maintain an unhealthy status quo. The reversed Tower reminds you that resistance can make matters more difficult. When a foundation is unstable, continuing to build on it can make an eventual collapse more severe. This card can also represent recovering from upheaval or trauma: the process may be slow, but rebuilding has begun. The reversed Tower encourages you not to fear necessary change and to accept that some things need to end. Rather than resist what cannot be avoided, you may choose to make changes proactively and transform things in a more manageable way.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Sudden Collapse","Shocking Revelation","Destruction and Rebuilding","False Structures Falling","Liberation and Awakening"],"reversed":["Avoiding Upheaval","Slow Breakdown","Fear of Change","Recovery and Rebuilding","Resisting the Truth"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Tower represents sudden upheaval and a startling moment of awakening. Lightning strikes the tower, symbolizing a forceful break through false structures and illusions. Your world may be shaken as beliefs, relationships, or systems built on unstable foundations begin to fall apart. This can be painful, but it may also be necessary. The Tower does not destroy what is genuine; it exposes what is false or unstable. This can feel like a forced awakening when change has been resisted for too long. The Tower reminds you that sometimes an entire system needs to be dismantled and rebuilt. In the ruins, you may see truths that were hidden. The breakdown can be the beginning of release.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Tower suggests that you may be avoiding or delaying a necessary breakdown. You sense the foundations shaking, yet try to prevent or control what is happening. The disruption may unfold more slowly or less dramatically, or you may already be recovering from a painful upheaval. Fear of change may be keeping you attached to a status quo that is barely holding together. The reversed Tower reminds you that delay can make an eventual collapse more difficult. Continuing to build on an unstable foundation carries risks. Sometimes the braver choice is to dismantle what is not working before it falls on its own. This card can also mark gradual progress as you rebuild after a difficult experience."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forceful downward impact","type":"Destruction and clearing","description":"The Tower''s energy is explosive and disruptive, like a sudden flash of lightning. It breaks down old structures and clears obstacles. Though startling, this energy can also bring release, striking forcefully from above."},"timing":{"speed":"Sudden and rapid","description":"The Tower points to a sudden event that may unfold within one to two weeks, though its timing cannot be predicted with certainty. The disruption may happen quickly, while rebuilding can take longer—often three to six months or more."},"advice":{"upright":"Do not cling to a structure that is no longer stable. Release your attachment to what is falling away and face the change. Look for truth and new possibilities amid the disruption. This is not necessarily the end; it can be the beginning of rebuilding. Give yourself time to recover without defining yourself only by what happened.","reversed":"If you sense a breakdown coming, consider facing the situation proactively instead of resisting it. Examine whether your foundations are sound; if they are not, making a deliberate change may be better than waiting for a collapse. If you are already rebuilding, keep moving one step at a time. Do not try to restore a structure that has already fallen if it no longer serves you."},"chakra":{"primary":"Whole-system reset","issue":"Your entire energy system may feel shaken and in need of rebuilding and realignment.","healingNote":"The Tower represents a deep reset that can affect the whole energy system. After upheaval, you may need time and support to regain your footing, starting with a sense of safety and grounding. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders while rebuilding stability. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this collapse may be a necessary blessing. The tower that held you back for so long may need to come down. In the ruins, you may discover a more authentic version of yourself. Do not assume that losing an old structure means losing everything; you can rebuild with greater honesty and stability. This can be a forceful release—meet it with courage.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that collapse cannot always be prevented, and delay can make it more difficult. If the foundation is unstable, it may be wiser to dismantle and rebuild intentionally. Or perhaps your soul is saying: you have been through upheaval, and you are still here. Now you can rebuild. Do not recreate the old tower; build something more honest and real."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '17-star', 'en', 'The Star', '星星', '{"keywords":["Hope","Faith","Inspiration","Serenity","Renewal"],"arcana":"major","number":17}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Star represents hope, faith, and spiritual renewal. Often appearing after the Tower, it symbolizes finding light and direction again after darkness and upheaval. When the Star appears, it brings an energy of calm, healing, and optimism. This can be a time to reconnect with your spirituality, restore confidence, and look toward the future. The Star encourages you to trust your sense of guidance and hold on to hope through difficult moments. It also represents inspiration, creativity, and connection with your higher self. Its energy is clear and peaceful, reminding you that quiet moments can hold strength. This may be a time to tend to old wounds, regain vitality, and become open to a brighter future. The Star illuminates the path ahead and reminds you not to give up hope; dawn can follow even a long night.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Star suggests that you may be going through a period of hopelessness, shaken faith, or lack of direction. You may feel discouraged and unable to see light ahead. This card can also point to feeling disconnected from your spirituality or losing a sense of meaning. Self-doubt and negative thoughts may be making it hard to recognize your potential and worth. The reversed Star reminds you that hope can still exist in dark moments. Do not let a temporary setback destroy your faith in yourself. This is a time to reconnect with your inner light. Seek out what inspires and uplifts you, whether that is nature, art, or spiritual practice. Losing hope can be temporary; you can take steps to rekindle it. Keep faith that light can return.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Renewed Hope","Spiritual Healing","Clear Faith","Guiding Inspiration","Peaceful Renewal"],"reversed":["Lost Hope","Shaken Faith","Spiritual Exhaustion","Self-Doubt","Feeling Directionless"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Star represents finding hope again after a period of darkness. Often following the Tower, it suggests that calm and healing may come after disruption and confusion. The Star brings clear hope, spiritual renewal, and renewed confidence in the future. This can be a time to reconnect with your spirituality and rebuild your faith. Its energy is gentle and restorative, like fresh water tending to a wound. The card reminds you that starlight can still be seen after the darkest night. The Star points to an authentic part of you that remains open, hopeful, and connected to a larger whole. It encourages you to keep faith and remain open to what may unfold. This may also be a period when inspiration and creativity begin to return. Your healing process can begin one small step at a time.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Star suggests hopelessness, shaken faith, or spiritual exhaustion. The darkness may feel so heavy that you cannot see any light. Hope can seem obscured, leaving you without direction or a sense of meaning. You may be overwhelmed by self-doubt and negative thoughts, unable to believe that things can improve. This card can also point to feeling spiritually disconnected, empty, or lost. The reversed Star reminds you that the light may be obscured without being gone. Even if you cannot see hope right now, it may still be there. This is a time to rebuild faith and look for meaning in small ways. Begin with simple steps that help you reconnect with your inner light. The reversed Star can also caution against optimism that is detached from practical reality."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Healing flow from above","type":"Receiving and renewal","description":"The Star''s energy is like healing water flowing down from the sky: gentle, nourishing, and renewing. It is clear, peaceful, and hopeful, soft yet enduring like starlight. Energy flows from the larger universe toward the earth, offering spiritual nourishment."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow healing","description":"The Star represents a period of healing and recovery that cannot be rushed. Renewal takes time and may unfold over two to six months. Allow yourself a quiet period to recover and let hope return gradually."},"advice":{"upright":"Keep room for hope and faith. This is a time for healing, so give yourself space to recover. Reconnect with your spirituality and seek out what inspires you. Remain open to a brighter future, and spend time in nature if it helps you feel restored.","reversed":"Do not let hopelessness consume you. Light may still be present even when you cannot see it. Rebuild faith through small things: a moment of gratitude or a beautiful experience. Seek support; you do not have to face the dark alone. Reconnect with your spirituality in ways that feel genuine to you."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Feeling disconnected from a larger source of meaning (Crown Chakra), or unable to express your authentic self (Throat Chakra).","healingNote":"The Star relates to the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual connection, and the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression. If you have lost hope or cannot express yourself, these centers may need care. Selenite and aquamarine can be included in personal reflective practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the darkest part of the night may be behind you. Starlight can help illuminate your path, and healing may already be underway. You do not have to force anything; stay open and allow hope to return in its own time. Your essential nature can still be clear and full of light. Remember this when you feel lost.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that despair can pass and hope can return. Not feeling the starlight does not mean it is gone. Loosen your grip on doubt and make room to believe that good things are still possible. The darkness you are experiencing is not all that you are; there is light within you too. Take your time, let hope return gradually, and do not give up."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '18-moon', 'en', 'The Moon', '月亮', '{"keywords":["Illusion","Intuition","Subconscious","Fear","Mystery"],"arcana":"major","number":18}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Moon represents illusion, the subconscious, and the realm of inner fears. Its hazy moonlit scene suggests that things may not be as they appear. When this card appears, you may be in a period of uncertainty and confusion, with some truths hidden or distorted. The Moon encourages you to explore your subconscious and face fears and shadow parts within. It also represents intuition, dreams, and deeper layers of the mind. Its energy is mysterious and powerful, drawing attention to what is hidden or unknown. This is a time to listen to your intuition and find the courage to face inner fears. Do not be misled by appearances; look carefully for what is real. The Moon reminds you that some things need to develop in the dark before they can be revealed at the right time.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Moon suggests that illusions may be fading and the truth beginning to emerge. You may be moving out of confusion and gradually seeing what is really happening. This card can also indicate that you are releasing long-suppressed fears and anxiety and beginning to face your shadow. However, the reversed Moon may also mean that fear still has a hold on you or that you are avoiding messages from your subconscious. You may be suppressing emotions and intuition while trying to control everything with reason. The reversed Moon asks you not to ignore your inner voice and feelings. Give yourself time and space to process complicated emotions instead of demanding immediate clarity. Sometimes accepting uncertainty and ambiguity is necessary. As time passes, more may become clear. Trust your intuition as one source of guidance through the fog.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Fog of Illusion","Subconscious Exploration","Intuitive Guidance","Emerging Fears","Hidden Mysteries"],"reversed":["Truth Coming to Light","Finding a Way Through the Fog","Releasing Fear","Growing Clarity","Avoiding Intuition"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Moon leads into the mysterious realm of the subconscious, where illusion can obscure what is real. The moonlit scene is unclear, reflecting a period of uncertainty or confusion. This card reminds you that appearances may not tell the whole story and that deeper exploration may be needed. The Moon represents the subconscious, dreams, intuition, and also the fears and shadows within. This is a time to face the unknown and listen to your intuition. The Moon may not provide clear answers; it asks you to move carefully through ambiguity, using your felt sense as well as reason. It can also point to deception, illusion, or projections. The Moon reminds you that what is forming in darkness may need time to emerge. Do not force clarity before it is ready; allow some mystery to remain.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Moon often suggests that illusions are beginning to fade and the truth is becoming clearer. You may be finding your way out of confusion and releasing fears or anxiety that have been suppressed for a long time. This can be a constructive shift toward greater awareness. However, the reversed Moon can also point to avoiding or denying messages from your subconscious. You may use reason to suppress intuition or refuse to face your fears. The card reminds you that clarity can come from facing the darkness rather than avoiding it. Sometimes it is wiser to accept uncertainty than to force an answer. The Moon''s wisdom is not always about understanding everything; it can also be about learning to trust your perception while you wait for more to emerge."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Tidal ebb and flow","type":"Subconscious fluctuation","description":"The Moon''s energy fluctuates like tides responding to the lunar cycle. It is mysterious, ambiguous, and emotional, not easily grasped through reason alone. Energy moves between conscious and subconscious states, bringing dreams, feelings, and shifting perceptions."},"timing":{"speed":"Unclear and shifting","description":"The Moon represents uncertain timing, with matters still hidden or confusing. It may take one to three months for the fog to clear. Avoid rushing into a decision; allow more information and understanding to emerge over time."},"advice":{"upright":"Trust your intuition even when you cannot see the whole picture. Do not rush a decision; give yourself time to observe and feel. Write down your dreams if that helps you reflect on your subconscious. Face your fears rather than letting them grow unseen, and make room for uncertainty.","reversed":"If the truth is emerging, allow yourself to acknowledge it, even if it is uncomfortable. If you have been avoiding your intuition, pause and listen inwardly. Make room for fears and emotions you have been suppressing. As the fog lifts, rebuild trust in your own perceptions."},"chakra":{"primary":"Third Eye Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Fear may cloud intuition (Third Eye Chakra), or emotions may feel difficult to regulate (Sacral Chakra).","healingNote":"The Moon relates to the Third Eye Chakra, associated with intuition, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with emotion. If you feel confused or overwhelmed by fear, these centers may need balance. Moonstone and labradorite can be included in personal practices for reflection and grounding. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that not every truth can be understood immediately. Some things need to develop in darkness and take shape amid uncertainty. Your fear is not necessarily an enemy; it may be a message waiting to be understood. Trust your intuition, even when it leads you into unfamiliar territory. The Moon''s light may be faint, but it can still help you notice the next part of the path.","reversed":"Your soul is celebrating as the fog begins to lift and you start to see more clearly. Or your soul may be reminding you to stop avoiding what you already know. Your intuition may have been pointing toward the truth, even if you have not wanted to hear it. Face your fears and move beyond denial. Clarity can come from having the courage to see what is there, including what you would rather not see."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '19-sun', 'en', 'The Sun', '太陽', '{"keywords":["Joy","Success","Vitality","Positivity","Celebration"],"arcana":"major","number":19}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Sun represents joy, success, and uncomplicated happiness. It is one of the most positive cards in the Tarot, symbolizing light, warmth, and vitality. When the Sun appears, it points toward a brighter period in which your efforts may be rewarded and success may be within reach. The Sun illuminates what was hidden, bringing clarity, truth, and insight. This can be a lively, confident, and optimistic time, well suited to expressing your authentic self and enjoying what life has to offer. The Sun also represents childlike openness, innocence, and simple happiness, reminding you to keep your heart sincere and receptive. It encourages you to celebrate accomplishments, share joy, and approach life with a positive attitude. The Sun''s energy is generous and nourishing, supporting growth. This is a time to appreciate what has come to fruition, give thanks for the good in your life, and look ahead with hope.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Sun is usually still positive, but may point to temporary clouds or joy that is delayed. You may feel low on energy, less confident, or unable to fully enjoy a success. This card can also caution against excessive optimism or overlooking a problem. You may be seeing a situation through rose-colored glasses instead of assessing it realistically. The reversed Sun reminds you that light can still be present during difficult moments, even when clouds temporarily obscure it. Do not let a setback diminish your confidence or optimism. Look for positive things in daily life, even if they seem small. Reconnect with your own sources of joy and vitality rather than letting outside circumstances determine your happiness. Remember that clouds can pass. Be patient and keep faith in the possibility of better days.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Pure Joy","Achievement","Vitality","Authentic Self","Radiant Clarity"],"reversed":["Temporary Clouds","Excessive Optimism","Delayed Joy","Low Confidence","Overlooking the Shadow"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Sun represents life''s purest joy and the visible expression of success. It shines generously on all things, symbolizing abundance, warmth, and vitality at their height. This card brings clarity, truth, and strongly positive energy. It can mark a harvest period when your efforts are rewarded and progress is clear. The Sun represents your authentic self: open, lively, and unafraid to be seen. Its joy is simple and wholehearted. Under the Sun, things become easier to see and there is less room for concealment. The upright Sun encourages you to express yourself confidently, celebrate your achievements, and share your happiness. Enjoy this bright moment and remember that you deserve to appreciate what is good in your life.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Sun is usually still positive, though its light may be temporarily obscured. You may feel less energetic or confident, or find it difficult to enjoy a success fully. There may be a delay, a temporary setback, or an inner cloud affecting your outlook. You may be overly optimistic and overlooking practical concerns, or seeing things through rose-colored glasses. This card can also point to fear of showing your authentic self or inner shadows that still need care. The reversed Sun reminds you that sunlight remains even when clouds cover it. Do not let temporary difficulties take all your joy away. Look for what is still bright, and rebuild your confidence and vitality. The clouds can part in time."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Radiating outward","type":"Expansion and generosity","description":"The Sun''s energy radiates outward, freely giving light and warmth. It is abundant, warm, and full of vitality, illuminating and nourishing what it touches. This energy is open, positive, and generous."},"timing":{"speed":"Rapid progress and clarity","description":"The Sun points to clear, relatively quick progress. Joy or a successful result may appear within one to four weeks. This can be a harvest period when the results of earlier effort are ready to be enjoyed."},"advice":{"upright":"Enjoy this positive period and celebrate what you have achieved. Share your happiness, express your authentic self with confidence, and do not hide your light. Give thanks for what you have. This can be a good time for creative and purposeful action.","reversed":"Look for what is still positive, even if it seems small. Do not let a temporary difficulty erase your optimism. Rebuild your confidence and remember your worth, while also checking whether excessive optimism is keeping you from seeing a real concern. Clouds can pass; keep perspective."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Heart Chakra","issue":"Low personal power or confidence (Solar Plexus Chakra), or a closed heart that makes it difficult to feel joy (Heart Chakra).","healingNote":"The Sun relates to the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power, and the Heart Chakra, associated with joy and connection. If you feel low in energy or unable to enjoy things, gentle practices that support these centers may help. Citrine and orange calcite can be included in personal reflection rituals. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is celebrating: you have come through darkness into the light. This joy is a result of your effort, and you deserve to enjoy it. Do not make yourself smaller; let yourself shine. Your light does not diminish others and may help illuminate the way for them too. Remember this moment if you face darkness again: light can return.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that the Sun is still there, even when temporarily obscured. Do not let a passing cloud make you forget your own light. You have an inner capacity for brightness and joy that difficulty cannot erase. Reconnect with your inner Sun; it is still there, waiting to be remembered. You deserve good things, and you can hold on to that belief."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '20-judgement', 'en', 'Judgement', '審判', '{"keywords":["Awakening","Reflection","Forgiveness","Decision","Rebirth"],"arcana":"major","number":20}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Judgement represents awakening, reflection, and an important moment of decision. The angel''s trumpet calls sleeping souls to rise, symbolizing an inner calling and a summons toward a higher purpose. When Judgement appears, it asks you to review past experiences, learn from them, and make an important choice. This is a time for honest self-reflection and looking carefully at your life, actions, and decisions. Judgement also represents forgiveness, atonement, and renewal, encouraging you to release past mistakes and regrets and offer yourself and others another chance. The card can bring clear insight and a broader understanding of patterns and meaning in your life. Judgement asks you to listen to your inner calling and respond to what feels purposeful and true. This is a time of transformation and growth, preparing you to welcome a new beginning.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Judgement card suggests that you may be avoiding self-reflection or finding it difficult to forgive yourself or others. Guilt, shame, or self-criticism may be keeping you tied to past mistakes. This card can also indicate ignoring an inner calling or refusing to respond to a larger purpose. Fear of change or reluctance to take responsibility may cause you to miss an important opportunity. The reversed Judgement asks you to face yourself honestly rather than avoid necessary reflection and evaluation. Forgiveness can be a key to release, whether you are forgiving another person or yourself. Let go of harsh judgment and meet your past with compassion and understanding. Learn from experience without allowing it to define you. Listen to your inner voice and respond to what life is asking of you, even if you feel uncertain or afraid.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Spiritual Awakening","Self-Reflection","Forgiveness and Release","Answering a Calling","Renewal and Transformation"],"reversed":["Avoiding Evaluation","Difficulty Forgiving","Ignoring a Calling","Self-Criticism","Missed Opportunity"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Judgement marks a moment of spiritual awakening and an inner call. The angel''s trumpet symbolizes a summons from a higher awareness, inviting you to respond to a purpose that feels true. This card asks you to review the past, reflect on experience, learn what you can, and make an important decision. It can be a time to reckon with past choices and awaken to what matters now. Judgement represents forgiveness: letting go of mistakes and regrets, and making room for a fresh start. This is a moment of renewal, when an old sense of self can give way to a new one. Judgement is not punishment; it is an opportunity for release and growth. It reminds you that you can answer your inner calling and prepare for a new chapter.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Judgement suggests that you may be avoiding necessary self-reflection or evaluation. You may be unable to forgive yourself or others and feel caught in guilt, shame, or resentment. The inner call may be ignored or refused because you fear change or greater responsibility. This card can also point to harsh self-criticism and difficulty accepting that you have made mistakes. The reversed Judgement reminds you that forgiveness can be a key to release. You cannot change the past, but you can choose how to meet it now. Be honest about mistakes without allowing them to define you. Listen to your inner calling even if you feel afraid or uncertain. This may be a time to make an important decision instead of postponing it."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Rising and elevating","type":"Awakening and renewal","description":"Judgement''s energy rises, like a soul waking from sleep and answering a higher call. It brings transformation, elevation, renewal, clear insight, and the possibility of a new beginning. Energy moves from an old sense of self toward a new one."},"timing":{"speed":"A decisive moment","description":"Judgement points to an important turning point that may unfold within one to three months. This can be a time for evaluation and decision-making. Circumstances may be ready for a choice and its consequences to be faced."},"advice":{"upright":"Review your past honestly and learn from it without becoming attached to regret. Forgive yourself and others where you can, and release what you are ready to put down. Listen to your inner calling and take responsibility for the purpose you choose. Meet a new beginning with courage.","reversed":"Stop avoiding yourself and look honestly at what is happening. Forgiveness is a form of release, not weakness. You may be judging yourself too harshly; accept that being human includes making mistakes. Listen for the inner call toward a more meaningful direction, and do not keep postponing a decision that is ready to be made."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Difficulty receiving an inner or spiritual calling (Crown Chakra), or speaking up for what you believe is true (Throat Chakra).","healingNote":"Judgement relates to the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual awareness, and the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression. If it is difficult to hear an inner calling or forgive, these centers may need care. Selenite and lapis lazuli can be included in personal reflective practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is calling you: the time has come. You have learned from what you have been through, and now you can gather that wisdom and take responsibility for your purpose. Release the past, offer forgiveness, and move bravely toward what matters to you. You are being called to do something meaningful; do not underestimate yourself. A new beginning is already underway—meet it with openness.","reversed":"Your soul is asking you to stop avoiding and punishing yourself. You cannot change the past, but you can choose to forgive and release it. Your inner calling is growing louder; how long will you pretend not to hear it? Your purpose is waiting, but begin by accepting and forgiving yourself. It may be time to answer."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '21-world', 'en', 'The World', '世界', '{"keywords":["Completion","Achievement","Fulfillment","Integration","Success"],"arcana":"major","number":21}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The World represents completion, achievement, and fulfillment. As the final card of the Major Arcana, it symbolizes the end of an important journey and the realization of a whole. When the World appears, you may have reached an important milestone, achieved a long-term goal, and integrated what you have learned. This is a time to celebrate success and enjoy the results of your efforts. The World also represents wholeness and unity: different parts of your life may be coming together in harmony. This card brings satisfaction, accomplishment, and inner peace. It encourages you to recognize your achievements and feel proud of how far you have come. At the same time, an ending can also be a beginning: one cycle is complete and another is about to open. Enjoy the present sense of fulfillment while staying open to new possibilities and adventures.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed World suggests that you may feel incomplete or not yet have reached a goal. You may be close to finishing but unable to cross the finish line for some reason. This card can point to a lack of closure, unresolved matters, or a delayed goal. You may have set unrealistic standards and feel dissatisfied, making it difficult to enjoy what you have already accomplished. The reversed World asks you to examine what is preventing you from completing this journey. Is it an outside obstacle or an inner fear? Sometimes fear of success or of the emptiness afterward can lead to self-sabotage. This card encourages you to overcome the final obstacle and finish what you started. It also asks you to appreciate the process, not only the outcome. Even if you have not reached your ultimate goal, you have already come a long way and deserve to recognize that effort.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Full Achievement","Integrated Wholeness","Journey Completed","A World of Possibilities","Fulfillment"],"reversed":["Unfinished Business","Lack of Closure","Stalled at the Threshold","Difficulty Celebrating","Unrealistic Standards"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the World represents the completion and fulfillment of the Major Arcana journey. After many experiences, the Fool reaches a moment of integration and wholeness. This card marks the close of an important journey, achievement of a goal, and a chance to celebrate success. The World symbolizes balance among the four elements and the integration of different parts of life into a harmonious whole. This is a time to gather the results of your effort and feel a deep sense of satisfaction and completion. The World encourages you to celebrate what you have achieved and recognize how far you have come. It also reminds you that every ending opens into a new beginning. One cycle is complete, and another is about to unfold. New possibilities and a larger journey may be waiting for you.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the World suggests that you may feel incomplete or have not yet reached a goal. You may be close to finishing but unable to cross the finish line. There may be unresolved matters, a lack of closure, or a delay. Unrealistic standards can leave you dissatisfied and unable to enjoy what you have already done. This card can also point to fear of the emptiness that may follow completion, leading to self-sabotage. The reversed World reminds you that completion does not require perfection. Ask what is holding you back: an outside obstacle or an inner fear? Recognize how far you have already come, even if the goal is not fully reached. Sometimes the process itself is an achievement. Let yourself pause, celebrate, and rest before beginning the next journey."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"A complete cycle","type":"Integration and completion","description":"The World''s energy is whole and complete, like a perfect circle. Its elements coexist in harmony and its many aspects are integrated. This is the energy of balance, completion, and realization, marking the close of one cycle and the beginning of another."},"timing":{"speed":"A moment of completion","description":"The World marks the end of a journey and suggests that circumstances may be ripe for completion. A milestone may arrive within one to three months. This is a time to gather results and celebrate as one important phase ends and another begins."},"advice":{"upright":"Celebrate what you have achieved and acknowledge the path you have taken. Enjoy this moment of fulfillment and be grateful for what you have learned and experienced. Stay open to what comes next; a new journey may be beginning. You have integrated a great deal, and you can take that experience into your next adventure.","reversed":"Look at what is keeping you from completing the journey. Are your standards too high, or are you afraid of the emptiness that may follow? Recognize what you have already accomplished instead of dismissing your effort because the goal is not fully complete. Sometimes the final step is letting go of perfectionism."},"chakra":{"primary":"Whole-system integration, especially the Crown and Root connection","issue":"Difficulty integrating spiritual and material life, or a lack of harmonious flow among the energy centers.","healingNote":"The World represents integration and balance throughout the energy system, connecting the Root Chakra with the Crown Chakra, earth with sky, and practical life with spiritual meaning. If you feel incomplete or out of balance, a whole-system approach to grounding and reflection may help. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders of integration and balance. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is celebrating: you did it. You completed this journey and learned what you came here to learn. You have integrated your experiences and become more whole. Enjoy this moment of fulfillment; you deserve joy and a sense of accomplishment. Remember, this is not the end, but a meaningful completion before a new beginning. A wider world is waiting to be explored.","reversed":"Your soul is gently asking: why can you not celebrate what you have achieved? You have come so far, so why does it still feel like not enough? Release perfectionism and recognize that you have completed an important part of the journey. Or perhaps your soul is encouraging you: you are at the final step, so do not give up. Whatever the case, you are already enough."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '1', 'en', 'Existence', '存在', '{"subtitle":"Existence"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a state of complete ease and oneness with the universe. This is the energy of simply existing: you do not need to become anyone; you can just be. In this moment, you are experiencing a deep, essential joy, like a cloud drifting freely across the sky without a purpose or agenda. Your energy is expanding and resonating with everything around you. This is not an escape from reality, but a return to your most authentic state. When you stop chasing, you may discover that you are already home.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to stop striving and simply be. You do not need to prove or accomplish anything. Let yourself settle into this moment and feel life''s natural flow. The universe is not asking you to do anything; it is inviting you to be. Each breath can be a celebration, and each moment can be complete in itself. Release plans and expectations for a while, and let life express itself through you. When you stop struggling, you may find that new possibilities arise naturally.","emotionalInsight":"Your anxiety may come from trying to become someone instead of accepting who you are now. Deep down, you may already be more whole than you realize. Loosening your attachment to the future can allow your emotions to settle. You have been looking outside yourself for approval and overlooking the abundance already within. Some fears and worries may be stories created by the mind. When you return to simple awareness, emotions can be experienced as passing visitors while you remain the steady center that notices them.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are always doing and have forgotten how to simply be. The problem may not be outside you; you may have lost touch with the ease of existing without striving. Stop chasing, and an answer may arise on its own. The mind can keep creating problems and then trying to solve them in an endless cycle. A breakthrough may come not from finding one more answer, but from noticing that the problem itself may be less solid than it seems. When you relax into the present, some of the knots can begin to loosen because they were never as fixed as they appeared.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and notice the movement of your breath. You do not need to change anything; simply observe. Feel your body and its connection with the space around you. You are part of existence itself. Let awareness spread through your whole body and notice the life in each cell. Now allow that awareness to extend beyond the body''s boundaries and into the surrounding space. You are not separate from everything around you; you are part of the whole. In this space there is no problem to solve and no answer to chase, only stillness."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '2', 'en', 'Inner Voice', '內在聲音', '{"subtitle":"Inner Voice"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your inner world is asking for your attention. This is a time to listen inwardly; your intuition may be trying to share something important. Trust that quiet inner voice. Amid the noise of the world, your soul has been speaking softly, waiting for you to pause and listen. This energy invites you back to inner stillness, where the answers you have been seeking may already be waiting. Rather than searching outside yourself, remember that wisdom can be found within.","dailyGuidance":"Today, make some quiet space to listen to your inner wisdom. There is a lot of noise around you, so take a break from outside distractions and notice what your heart is saying. Give yourself time alone, away from social media, other people''s opinions, and outside expectations. In stillness, your intuition may become easier to hear. When making a decision today, do not ask everyone else first; check in with yourself. Your inner sense can help you discern what feels right for you, so give it room to speak.","emotionalInsight":"Emotional turbulence may arise when you ignore your inner voice. You may keep seeking outside advice and approval while forgetting that some of the truest answers are already within you. When you feel confused or anxious, it may be because your actions do not align with your inner guidance. Those uneasy feelings can be a reminder that you have moved away from your own path. Try listening for what your emotions are communicating; they can be guides to understanding what matters to you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may be unable to move forward because you are listening to other people instead of yourself. The block may be a lack of trust in your own intuition. As you learn to trust your inner guidance, your path may become clearer. You may fear making the wrong decision and keep looking for outside approval, but this can leave you feeling even more lost. The deeper block may not be a lack of information, but a lack of trust in yourself. When you begin to listen to your own wisdom, obstacles can look different and you may find a direction that feels like your own true north.","meditationEntry":"Find a quiet place and rest a hand over your heart. Ask yourself, “What is my heart trying to tell me?” Do not analyze; simply listen and allow an answer to emerge in its own way. Feel the rhythm of your heartbeat, the pulse of life. There is space between each breath, and in that space you can make room for inner wisdom. Do not rush to find an answer; stay open and receptive. When you become truly quiet, your inner voice may become clearer. It might arrive as a feeling, an image, or a simple knowing."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '3', 'en', 'Playfulness', '遊戲', '{"subtitle":"Playfulness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your energy is calling for lightness and play. Life does not have to be so serious; this may be a moment to let your inner child come out and enjoy the simple joy of being alive. Perhaps it has been a long time since you truly laughed or felt carefree. This card reminds you that life can be a celebration, not only a list of tasks. Set down your responsibilities for a little while, even if only briefly, and reconnect with the part of you that knows how to play.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s reminder is not to take everything so seriously. Meet life with a playful spirit and you may discover more possibilities and creativity. Even work can sometimes be approached as a game. When you relax, inspiration may come more easily. Try doing something today without a goal, simply because it brings you joy: dance, sing, draw, or take a walk. Let a sense of lightness return, and you may find it easier to see new ways to approach a problem.","emotionalInsight":"Your heaviness may come from taking life too seriously. Loosen the frame of what you think you must do and allow yourself a little ease. Joy does not always need a reason. You may be carrying the weight of the world as though everything would fall apart if you stopped trying so hard. Yet life may flow more easily when you allow yourself to relax. Some things you treat as grave obligations may be mental cages. When you meet them with a playful perspective, they may lose some of their power over you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are treating life like an exam instead of an exploration. Loosen your attachment to outcomes and approach things with a spirit of play; new paths may open. Being preoccupied with right and wrong, winning and losing, can keep you from moving. Creativity and breakthroughs often need room to experiment. When you are less afraid of mistakes and imperfection, you may feel freer. The block may not be that you have not tried hard enough; you may be trying too hard. Relax and let yourself explore.","meditationEntry":"Remember a game you loved as a child and reconnect with the uncomplicated joy you felt. Let that energy move through your body. Feel the freedom of being fully present, with no past to revisit and no future to plan—only the joy of this moment. Let your body move without needing a reason, simply because it wants to. Allow a smile to arise naturally. In this space, you do not need to become anyone; you can simply enjoy being alive."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '4', 'en', 'The Rebel', '叛逆者', '{"subtitle":"The Rebel"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your rebellious spirit is awakening. This is a time to question old patterns and break out of limiting frames. You may no longer be willing to follow rules that do not belong to you. This energy is wild, free, and hard to contain. You are beginning to see through the supposed shoulds and musts that were never truly yours. This is not destruction for its own sake, but liberation. You are taking off masks that feel false and returning to a more original, untamed self. This can be a powerful moment of change.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to have the courage to be yourself. Do not compromise what is true for you just to please others. Real freedom comes from living honestly. If something feels uncomfortable or false today, it is all right to say no. If there is something you have wanted to do but held back for fear of judgment, consider taking a step toward it. You do not need to wait for permission to be your own authority. The world needs your authenticity, not your compliance. Stand up for yourself, even if doing so feels lonely for a while.","emotionalInsight":"Anger and unease may come from suppressing your authentic self. You may have been playing a role others expect while something in you pushes back. Listen to that resistance. Relationships, work, or ways of living that make you feel stifled may be telling you that this path does not fit. Your emotions are not necessarily the problem; they can be signals. Anger may point to strength, and restlessness may reflect a desire for change. Rather than suppressing these feelings, explore what they are asking of you; they may help you return to what is genuine.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you fear breaking rules or being rejected. Yet the deeper block may be that you have not allowed yourself to be free. When you give yourself permission to question the rules, new paths may appear. You may be too concerned with others'' opinions and afraid of losing love or belonging. But when you distort yourself to gain acceptance, you risk losing touch with who you are. A breakthrough may ask you to tolerate some loneliness, misunderstanding, or discomfort in order to live more truthfully. When you make that choice, you may find support in unexpected places.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a wall in front of you representing the rules and limits that hold you back. Now picture yourself walking through it. Feel the energy of freedom moving through you. The wall may represent your parents'' expectations, social standards, or limits you have absorbed. Look at it and ask: do you want to remain confined by it, or are you ready to move beyond it? Take a deep breath and feel the strength within you. You may be stronger than you think. Walk through the wall and into a life that feels more truly yours, where no one else can dictate how you must live."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '5', 'en', 'Aloneness', '孤獨', '{"subtitle":"Aloneness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a moment of deep solitude. This is not the same as loneliness; it can be an opportunity to connect deeply with yourself. In solitude, you may discover the richness within. This is a sacred space where you do not need to play a role or meet anyone else''s expectations. You can simply be yourself, fully. This energy invites you to stop looking outward for everything and return to your inner sanctuary. There, you may meet your most authentic self, the part of you that is not defined by being alone. Solitude can be a gift rather than a punishment.","dailyGuidance":"Make some time to be alone today. Do not fear your own company; solitude may help you discover what feels most true to you. This can be a nourishing moment for your inner life. Cancel a social plan if you need to, turn off your phone, and give yourself time that belongs only to you. Do not fill every moment with activity; spend some quiet time in your own company. In that space, you may hear an inner voice that is usually covered by noise. Practice enjoying time by yourself; it can be a deep form of self-care.","emotionalInsight":"A feeling of emptiness may come from looking outside yourself to fill it. Lasting contentment begins with your relationship with yourself. Learn to be with solitude rather than always escaping it. You may fear facing yourself, so you keep filling life with relationships, work, or entertainment. Yet these external things cannot always fill an inner space. When you are willing to sit with what feels empty, you may discover that it is not a void but a space full of possibility. Aloneness is not necessarily a lack; it can also be a sense of wholeness.","blockageAnalysis":"You may have difficulty moving forward because you fear being alone and rely heavily on outside connections. The block may be that you have not yet learned to be your own good companion. Embrace solitude and your strength may return. You may be spending a lot of energy maintaining relationships, pleasing others, and seeking connection while forgetting your relationship with yourself. Fear of being alone can keep you in unhealthy relationships. As you learn to enjoy your own company, you may feel stronger and less dependent on others to define you. This can be a form of freedom.","meditationEntry":"Sit in a quiet space and notice what it is like to be here on your own. You do not need anyone''s company; simply be with yourself. Feel the wholeness of this moment. Close your eyes and breathe deeply. Notice your existence, not as someone''s partner, friend, child, or parent, but simply as yourself. In this moment, you are whole; nothing is missing. Let the feeling of aloneness be present without resisting it. Within solitude there can be deep quiet and freedom. You can set down your masks and return to your essential self."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '6', 'en', 'The Lovers', '愛人', '{"subtitle":"The Lovers"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a moment of deep connection, whether with another person, with life, or with the receptive and active energies within yourself. This is the energy of love in motion—not possession, but meeting and blending. Your heart may be opening, allowing you to feel and give more fully. This energy invites you to lower your defenses and allow vulnerability, because genuine intimacy needs room for it. Love is not about finding perfection; it is about recognizing wholeness within imperfection. This can be a time of healing, as old hurts begin to soften in the light of love.","dailyGuidance":"Today is about connection. Whether you are deepening a relationship or bringing the receptive and active energies within yourself into greater harmony, be present and involved. Do not be afraid to show who you really are, including your vulnerability and imperfections. Real love does not require perfection; it asks for authenticity. Practice giving without expecting something in return. When you give from a sense of abundance rather than lack, love can flow more naturally. Remember that caring for yourself is part of being able to care for others.","emotionalInsight":"Your emotions may be telling you that it is time to open your heart. Past hurts may have led you to build high walls, but those walls can also keep love from entering. Allow yourself to risk feeling again. Even though being open can involve the possibility of hurt, it is also part of being alive. Your heart may long for connection and to be seen, understood, and accepted. Do not deny that need; it is not weakness. When you allow yourself to give and receive love, you reconnect with an essential part of life. Healing may be taking place; give the process time.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you fear being hurt again, so you have closed your heart. But a closed heart also has difficulty receiving love. A breakthrough may begin with a willingness to be vulnerable and take an emotional risk. You may be waiting for perfectly safe love, but intimacy involves letting go of some control. It is difficult to experience closeness while remaining completely guarded. The block may not be that you have not found the right person, but that you are still learning how to show up authentically. When you accept and care for all parts of yourself, including those you think are unworthy of love, some barriers may begin to fall.","meditationEntry":"Rest a hand over your heart and feel its rhythm. Imagine your heart as a lotus slowly opening, one petal with each breath. Do not force it; simply allow it. Notice past hurts without running away from them. You might thank them for what they have taught you about the depth of love. Now imagine a warm light rising from your heart and filling your chest. This is the energy of love; it has been here all along. Let this love flow toward yourself first, embracing every part of you. Then allow it to move outward naturally, toward the people and beings in your life."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '7', 'en', 'Patience', '耐心', '{"subtitle":"Patience"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is a time of waiting, but not passive waiting; it is an opportunity to be fully aware and present. The seed has been planted, and now it needs time to sprout. You cannot hurry a rose into bloom; you can offer sunlight and water, then trust the process. This energy teaches you that life has its own rhythm and forcing it can interfere with its natural unfolding. You are learning a deep lesson in trust. When you stop pushing, you may notice that life has its own way of moving forward. This is not giving up, but participating with greater awareness.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to slow down. Do not rush to see the result or reach the destination; the process itself has value. You may be hurrying so much that you forget to notice what is along the way. Practice waiting without anxiety and trusting without trying to control everything. When impatience arises, take a deep breath and remind yourself that things unfold in their own time. The universe may not follow your schedule, so stay open to the timing that is actually available. Finding calm while you wait can be a source of strength.","emotionalInsight":"Your anxiety may come from wanting results immediately. Life is not a microwave; it is more like a slow process of ripening. Impatience can reflect a lack of trust in the future or in yourself. Take a deep breath and return to the present. What you need may arrive in its own time, neither too early nor too late. The things that ask you to wait may be helping you prepare. If they arrived now, you might not yet be ready to receive them. Let waiting be an opportunity rather than a punishment.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are so eager for results that you interfere with the natural process. The deeper block may be pushing too hard instead of allowing things to unfold. When you learn to loosen your grip and trust life''s wisdom, a path may open more naturally. Trying to control the timing and outcome can create more resistance. A breakthrough may call for surrender—not giving up your effort, but releasing your attachment to a specific result. When you stop struggling against life and begin moving with it, new possibilities may emerge. Patience is not passive waiting; it is an active form of trust.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a tree. Feel your roots extending deep into the earth and drawing nourishment. Feel your branches reaching toward the sky and receiving sunlight. You do not need to hurry your growth; it happens in its own way. When spring arrives, flowers bloom without being forced. Now bring this awareness to your life. The things you are eager to see may be like seeds growing beneath the ground. You cannot see them, but growth may already be underway. Trust the process. With each breath, practice yielding to life''s rhythm. As you wait, you are also becoming more deeply yourself."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '8', 'en', 'Courage', '勇氣', '{"subtitle":"Courage"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are at a moment that may call for courage—not reckless bravery, but meeting fear with awareness. Real courage does not mean feeling no fear; it means continuing even when fear is present. An inner fire may be urging you beyond your comfort zone and into the unknown. This energy is raw, untamed, and difficult to suppress. It does not begin with a guaranteed outcome; it responds to a call for growth. You may be stronger than you think, and this can be a time to discover that for yourself. Step into the unknown with care and trust in your capacity to meet what comes.","dailyGuidance":"Today may call for a brave step. The thing you have been afraid of or the decision you have been postponing may need your attention. Do not wait for a perfect moment; it may never arrive. Courage is not waiting until fear disappears, but moving forward while acknowledging it. Do one thing that feels challenging: have a conversation, make a decision, or try something new. As you move through fear, you may discover greater freedom on the other side. Remember that you have already faced difficult things, and you have resources to meet this too.","emotionalInsight":"Your fears are real feelings, but they are not always facts. Fear is the mind''s response to the unknown, and the unknown is not automatically dangerous. You may be avoiding certain emotions, conversations, or truths, but avoidance can make fear grow. Face what you can, and you may find it less frightening than expected. Emotional turbulence may come from being caught between a familiar path that feels constricting and a new path that feels uncertain but freeing. Your heart may have a sense of direction while your mind resists. Listen inwardly and let courage grow alongside the fear.","blockageAnalysis":"Fear may be freezing you while you wait for guarantees that life cannot provide. A breakthrough may begin by acknowledging fear and taking a thoughtful step anyway. You may believe you have to overcome fear before acting, but sometimes confidence grows through action. The block may be less about ability than trust in yourself. You may already have resources you have not recognized. As you move through uncertainty without a perfect map, you may discover the next part of the path as you go. Courage is not the absence of fear; it is fear being present without having the final say.","meditationEntry":"Stand up and feel both feet firmly on the ground. Notice the earth supporting you. Imagine a door in front of you, with the unknown on the other side. Your fear may say, “Do not open it,” while another part of you may be ready to cross the threshold. Take a deep breath and feel your own strength. You are larger than this moment of fear. Reach out and open the door in your imagination. As you step across, notice any sense of freedom or possibility. Each time you face a fear, you can learn more about your strength. Carry that awareness into daily life, one step at a time."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '9', 'en', 'Completion', '完成', '{"subtitle":"Completion"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"A cycle is coming to a close, and this may be a time to gather what you have learned. You have traveled a long way; now there may be room to celebrate, integrate, and let go. Completion is not only an ending; it also creates space for a new beginning. This energy invites you to look back with gratitude and then release what is finished. Do not cling to what has already served its purpose and given you what you needed to learn. Empty your hands and make room to receive what comes next. Completion is an art: it asks you to let go with grace and trust that another chapter can unfold in its own time.","dailyGuidance":"Today is about endings and new beginnings. Look at your life and ask what has reached completion and what may need to be released. It could be a relationship, a job, a belief, or a habit. Consider giving it a clear ending instead of leaving it unresolved and draining your energy. You might write a letter, create a small ritual, or simply say goodbye inwardly. Be grateful for what it gave you, then let it go. This is also a day to celebrate how far you have come. You have done meaningful work. Clear some space for what may come next.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel some sadness, and that is natural. Endings often include a sense of loss, even when the ending is chosen. Allow the sadness; it is part of transition. At the same time, notice any relief or lightness as you put down a burden. Your emotions may include gratitude, grief, anticipation, and uncertainty; all of these can be natural responses to completion. Do not suppress them—let them move. An ending can feel like a small death, while also making room for renewal. Trust yourself to move through the transition at your own pace.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you cannot release something that has already ended. You may be attached to the past even though it no longer serves you. The deeper block may be fear of emptiness or of not knowing who you are without it. Yet letting go can make room for something new. You may be lingering in a relationship, job, or pattern because it is familiar, not because it is right for you. A breakthrough may begin with acknowledging that it has ended. Grieve it, appreciate what it gave you, and then release it. When you do, you may notice new doors opening.","meditationEntry":"Sit down and close your eyes. Look back on the journey you have taken, as if watching a film. Notice its highs and lows and how you have grown. Now offer a quiet thank-you for the experience. Feel whatever gratitude is present. Imagine placing the whole experience in a beautiful box and gently closing the lid. This is not forgetting; it is completion. Notice your hands empty and your heart spacious. This emptiness is not only loss; it can also be possibility. Take a deep breath, open your eyes, and meet the world in front of you with fresh attention."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '10', 'en', 'Change', '改變', '{"subtitle":"Change"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is moving, and everything is changing. Resisting this movement may not help; you can choose to move with it. This is a dynamic, fluid moment in which nothing is fixed forever. The energy invites you to loosen your attachment to stability and make room for impermanence. Change is not a threat; it is part of life''s nature. You may be shedding an old skin and growing into something new. The process can feel uncomfortable, but it may also be necessary. Instead of trying to hold on to what is leaving, open yourself to what is arriving. You are becoming someone new through this process.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to yield to change. Rather than trying to control or predict everything, stay responsive to what is unfolding. Life may be rearranging things, sometimes clearing away the old before something new can take shape. Trust the process even when you cannot yet see the direction. Practice flexibility today. When plans change, instead of only complaining, ask what the change might be showing you. A different possibility may be opening. Loosen your grip on control and allow life to surprise you. Change can be a companion rather than an enemy.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel uneasy because change can take away your sense of control. You want to know what will happen next, but life does not provide the whole script in advance. Uncertainty can stir fear. Look a little deeper: perhaps what you fear is not change itself, but losing an identity you have built around a role, a job, or a relationship. You are more than any one of those things. Change may be removing a mask and helping you see yourself more clearly. This can be frightening, but it may also bring freedom. Allow yourself to discover who you are becoming.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are resisting change that cannot be avoided. You want everything to stay as it was, but life keeps moving. The block may be that you are fighting the river instead of learning how to move with it. The more you resist, the more painful the struggle can become. A breakthrough may begin with accepting that change is already happening. You cannot prevent it, but you can choose how to respond. When you stop resisting and begin to cooperate with what is real, change may bring release rather than only loss. Let the old end so the new can take shape.","meditationEntry":"Imagine yourself standing beside a river. Its water keeps moving and is never exactly the same; this is one way to see life. Now imagine stepping into the river. At first, you try to hold your position and resist the current. Notice the struggle. Then relax and let the water carry you for a moment. Notice any sense of release. You do not need to know exactly where the river will take you; practice trust. Now notice your body and your life. Cells renew, thoughts move, and emotions change. Change is already part of being alive. As you accept this, fear may begin to loosen. You are part of the river too."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '11', 'en', 'Breakthrough', '突破', '{"subtitle":"Breakthrough"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be on the edge of a significant breakthrough. Your preparation and struggles may have been leading to this moment. This is a point where gradual change can become a different way of seeing or being. The energy can feel explosive, liberating, and difficult to reverse. You may not be able to return to the old state because you have begun to see a new possibility. This is not always a gradual shift; it can feel like a leap. Fear and excitement may be present together as you step into unfamiliar territory. A deeper part of you may recognize that this is the moment you have been waiting for.","dailyGuidance":"Today may be a day for action. The thing you have prepared for or the decision you have thought about for a long time may be ready for a next step. Instead of endlessly analyzing, consider what you can do now. A breakthrough can ask for courage and a willingness to change an old pattern, even before you know exactly what comes next. Allow yourself to take a reasonable risk and accept that success and failure are both possible. Sometimes a leap becomes possible when you stop trying to control every detail and take the next step. If you are ready, take it.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel a strong energy building inside you, as if a breakthrough is near. Excitement, fear, anticipation, and unease can all be present at once. That can be normal when moving from one state into another. Do not suppress these feelings; notice how they may be giving you energy to move. You may have been waiting for a perfect moment, but progress often begins when you are willing to move imperfectly. Your emotions may be telling you that something is ready to change; take time to listen and choose a grounded next step.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck at the threshold of a breakthrough, seeing a possibility but fearing the loss of familiar security. The block may be waiting for a guarantee, even though a breakthrough often involves uncertainty. You may need to take a first step before you know exactly how everything will unfold. You might think you are not ready, but readiness does not always arrive as certainty. As you move forward without knowing every detail, you can learn what the next step needs to be. Stop preparing endlessly and begin with one practical action. That can be the path through the threshold.","meditationEntry":"Stand up and notice the energy in you that wants to move beyond an old limit. You may feel it in your chest, abdomen, or limbs. Do not suppress it; allow yourself to notice it fully. Imagine a thin membrane in front of you, representing an old limitation. Look at it and feel what it brings up. Take a deep breath and imagine moving through it with your whole presence. Notice any feeling of release or openness on the other side. Carry that awareness into your life. You do not need to be perfect to begin; willingness is enough for one next step."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '12', 'en', 'Acceptance', '接受', '{"subtitle":"Acceptance"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is the energy of deep surrender—not giving up, but accepting reality as it is. You are learning a difficult lesson: not everything needs to be changed; some things first need to be acknowledged. Acceptance can bring peace because struggle eases when you stop resisting what is already true. It is not the same as approving of everything or giving in; it is seeing clearly. You cannot change the past or control other people, and life may not follow your script. But you can choose how to respond. As you accept what is real, you may find more freedom in deciding what to do next.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s practice is acceptance. Notice what in your life you have been resisting: a person, a situation, a fact, or a part of yourself. For today, stop fighting its present reality. This does not mean you have to like it or give up on taking action to change it; first, acknowledge that this is how things are right now. When you accept the facts, new energy may become available—energy that was tied up in resistance. For what you cannot change today, try saying, “I accept this as it is.” Then notice what choices remain open to you.","emotionalInsight":"Much of your pain may come from resisting reality. You want things to be different, the past not to have happened, other people to change, or yourself to be someone else. But reality is what it is. When you stop arguing with what has already happened, pain may shift toward greater calm. Acceptance is not surrendering your ability to act; it is acknowledging the facts. You can accept the present while still working toward a different future. Without accepting where you are now, you may remain caught in resistance and find it harder to move forward. Your emotions may be inviting you to put down the burden of how things should be and meet what is.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you refuse to accept some part of reality. A great deal of energy may be going into resistance rather than creation. The deeper block may be believing that acceptance means defeat, when it can be the beginning of effective action. When you see the current situation clearly, you can decide what can be changed and what cannot. Fighting an unchangeable fact can exhaust you. When you can say, “Yes, this is the situation right now,” a path forward may become easier to see. Acceptance does not have to keep you stuck; it can help you move with what is real. This is a paradox and a deep kind of wisdom.","meditationEntry":"Sit quietly and bring to mind something you have been resisting. Look at it without turning away. Notice the tension that resistance creates in your body. Take a deep breath, and as you exhale, say inwardly, “I accept this as it is.” Notice whether anything softens: your shoulders, your breath, or your heart. Say it again, not because you approve of everything, but because you are willing to see what is true now. Let a little calm move through you. This is the strength of surrender. In acceptance, you may find more freedom to choose your next step."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '13', 'en', 'Transformation', '轉化', '{"subtitle":"Transformation"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in the midst of a deep transformation. This is not a surface change but a shift in your very nature: an old version of you is ending while a new one is taking shape. The process may feel like being divided between two states—you are no longer who you were, but not yet fully who you will become. This is a moment of alchemy, in which pain, challenges, and confusion can become material for change. Do not try to hurry the process; it has its own timing. You are becoming something new.","dailyGuidance":"Today, allow transformation to happen. Do not cling to an old identity just because it feels safe. You are shedding an old skin; the process may be uncomfortable, but it can be necessary. Notice what may be ending: old beliefs, habits, or relationship patterns. Rather than trying to revive them, let them leave quietly. Also notice what is beginning to emerge: new perceptions, desires, and possibilities. Give them care even if you do not yet understand them completely. This is a day of transition; remain open.","emotionalInsight":"Feeling lost and confused can be a natural part of transformation. You may not know who you are or what you want, and that uncertainty can be part of the process. Old structures are dissolving before new ones have formed. Being in this open space can feel frightening, but it also holds possibilities. Do not force yourself to find a new identity immediately; give yourself time. Your emotions may fluctuate as you release what is old and make room for what is new. Trust the confusion as part of a process of renewal.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are holding on to an old identity while wanting a new life. It can be difficult to carry both at once. The block may be the fear that something in you has to end before you can be reborn. You may be afraid to release the person you think you are, though that identity may be only one role you have played. You are larger than that role. When you allow the old to end without clinging to it, transformation can continue. You may discover that what you lose is a limitation, while new possibilities open. First, be willing to step into the unknown.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a caterpillar forming a cocoon. Inside, your old shape dissolves and you no longer know what you are. This can feel frightening, but it is part of the passage. Notice the dissolving and the feeling of solid things becoming fluid. Do not resist; stay present with the transformation. Then imagine a new form beginning to take shape, entirely different from before. Wings emerge, and you become a butterfly. When you leave the cocoon, you are changed. Let yourself imagine flight as a natural expression of what you have become."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '14', 'en', 'Integration', '整合', '{"subtitle":"Integration"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is an energy of integration and balance. You have been through many experiences and learned a great deal; now it may be time to bring the pieces together. You do not have to choose one extreme when you can hold two opposites at once. This is a sign of maturity: being able to contain contradictions without feeling split apart. Your yin and yang, light and shadow, reason and emotion can each find a place. Integration does not erase differences; it allows them to coexist in harmony. You are becoming more whole.","dailyGuidance":"Today is a day for integration. Notice parts of your life that seem opposed: work and rest, giving and receiving, strength and softness, independence and connection. Rather than choosing one side, look for a point of balance. You can be both strong and gentle, both independent and close to others. Practice including rather than excluding. When you feel an inner conflict, do not suppress either side; let them have a conversation. You may discover that they are not enemies, but two aspects of a larger whole. Integrating them can help you feel more complete.","emotionalInsight":"You may have felt that you must choose: reason or emotion, strength or vulnerability. But life is not always an either-or question. You can contain many qualities at once. Emotional turbulence may arise when you suppress some parts of yourself and permit only others to be expressed. Now may be a time to let every part come home: your anger and compassion, your fear and courage, your shadow and your light. They are all part of you. As you integrate these parts, inner conflict may soften and a greater sense of peace can emerge.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are divided against yourself, fighting certain parts while trying to become a “better” version of yourself. You may not realize that the parts you reject can hold strength and wisdom too. The deeper block may be difficulty integrating opposites. When you stop dividing yourself into good and bad or right and wrong and begin accepting more of your whole experience, your energy may return. You may not need to become a different person; you may need to become more fully yourself. Integration can be a path back home.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and imagine two parts of yourself that have been pulling in different directions: perhaps your head and heart, your masculine and feminine energies, or your inner child and adult self. See them standing opposite one another. Invite them to move closer. There may be resistance, and that is all right; keep making room for them to meet. Imagine them joining into one whole presence. Feel any sense of completeness or coming home. This is you, with all your parts. Breathe deeply and let that wholeness settle through your body. You do not have to be divided; you can be one."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '15', 'en', 'Slowness', '緩慢', '{"subtitle":"Slowness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is inviting you to slow down—not because you are lazy, but because depth matters more than speed. In a fast-moving world, choosing slowness can be a way to return to what is essential. When you slow down, you may feel, see, and experience life more fully. This energy reminds you that what matters is not how fast you move, but whether you are truly traveling your own path. Slowness can help you savor life and make each moment more meaningful. You are not running away; you are arriving.","dailyGuidance":"Today, slow down intentionally. Walk a little more slowly, speak a little more slowly, and take your time eating. Notice what changes when you slow down: you may see more detail, feel your body, and hear your inner voice. This does not need to be a day for doing the most things, but it can be a day for doing each thing with greater care. Quality matters more than quantity. When you feel an urge to rush, pause and breathe. Ask yourself what you are hurrying toward and whether it is truly urgent. Give yourself permission to move at a gentler pace.","emotionalInsight":"Anxiety and haste may come from a belief that you must keep running to deserve your place in the world. That is not the measure of your worth. Your value is not only in your productivity; it is also in your existence. When you slow down, you may feel panic because you have learned to equate slowness with laziness. But beneath that fear may be a deep desire for rest, quiet, and permission to simply be without proving anything. Listen to that desire; it may come from a wise part of you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are always running but never feel that you have arrived. You may think speed will take you to your destination, while missing what is around you. The deeper block may be avoiding the present by filling every space with activity because inner quiet feels uncomfortable. Yet that quiet may be what you need. When you slow down and become more present in each moment, you may discover that arrival is not somewhere in the future. The destination can be found in the present. Slow down and come home to this moment.","meditationEntry":"Find a comfortable place to sit. Now slow your breathing, very gently. Breathe in for a count of six and out for a count of six, adjusting to what feels comfortable. Notice the details of each breath. Then move your hand slowly, as if it were moving through water. Feel the texture of the air and the movement of your muscles. Let everything slow down. In this slower pace, time may feel more spacious and each moment more expansive. You do not have to be chased by time. Let yourself rest in the present, one breath at a time."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
